      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "shaky",
        "addressCheck": "Partly supported, but the house number is contested across sources. The cited ynet article DOES place \"קהל חסידים\" at רוקח 20 and supports the demolition narrative. HOWEVER, atmag.co.il places \"קהל חסידים א'\" at רוקח 18 and \"מראות הסולם\" at רוקח 20 (built ~1889/1890), while go-arch.co.il and GuideStar register \"מראות הסולם\" at שמעון רוקח 18. The open web disagrees with itself on whether קהל חסידים is at 18 or 20; the research adopts ynet's \"20\" without flagging the conflict. Street name \"שמעון רוקח\" is correct. Glatter is SILENT — no entry for Shimon Rokach, Neve Tzedek, or \"קהל חסידים\" — so it neither supports nor contradicts the number. mapErrorFlag \"wrong-dynasty\" is appropriate.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed, with one seriously misattributed source. Source 1 (ynet L-3347055) is genuine, resolves, and supports the donor/split/sale/demolition narrative — load-bearing and it checks out. Source 3 (Hebrew Wikipedia \"בית שמעון רוקח\") is real but only supports the street-naming point (Shimon Rokach, founder of Neve Tzedek, d. 1922); silent on קהל חסידים. Source 2 (psakdin, Carmelovitch heqdesh) is a CONFLATION ERROR: that case concerns \"אגודת בית כנסת קהל חסידים נחלת שבעה\" at 13 Yoel Solomon St, JERUSALEM (Jerusalem Magistrate's Court 13955-08-10) — a different synagogue sharing the generic name, NOT the Neve Tzedek building. Better uncited sources exist (atmag, makorrishon, go-arch). Glatter's only Rokach is Belz/אהרן רוקח at אחד העם 1944 (different person/place/era).",
        "corrections": "1) REMOVE the psakdin source and the Carmelovitch heqdesh from the founder field — that heqdesh/case belongs to a different \"קהל חסידים\" at 13 Yoel Solomon St, Nahalat Shiva, JERUSALEM, not Neve Tzedek. Most serious conflation.\n2) FIX founder: ynet supports Huna Adler (חונא אדלר, to Cairo 1893) as DONOR; atmag credits Shimon Rokach himself (~1890). State as \"donor Huna Adler (ynet); possibly built by Shimon Rokach (atmag)\"; drop heqdesh-as-founder.\n3) FIX the \"1910 → מראות הסולם established\" claim — ANACHRONISM. \"מראות הסולם\" is named after R. Yehuda Ashlag's \"הסולם\" Zohar commentary (1943–1953; it even contains a section titled \"מראות הסולם\"). The building dates ~1889 but could not be NAMED \"מראות הסולם\" in 1910.\n4) FLAG the contested house number (18 vs 20); ynet's \"20\" for קהל חסידים is uncorroborated and reversed by atmag.\n5) NUANCE the surname \"coincidence\": Shimon Rokach is NOT Belz, but WAS from a Sadigura Hasidic family (grandfather R. Yosef Rokach). Both Rokachs are Hasidic, different courts — disambiguation stands, framing imprecise.\n6) Founding year \"~1888–1893\" is defensible from ynet's Adler-1893 anchor but conflicts with 1889/1890 elsewhere; widen and note.\n7) Retain the research's Glatter conclusion: no entry for this address; only Rokach is Belz at אחד העם 1944, a coincidental surname.",
        "dynastyCheck": "\"General Hasidic, no specific court\" is DEFENSIBLE and Glatter-consistent. Glatter has no entry for this address and no general \"קהל חסידים\" shtibel; its only Rokach is Belz / רבי אהרן רוקח at אחד העם, 1944 — different person, place, and a 30+ year-later context. The research correctly rejects Belz and disambiguates the street namesake. Over-reach: it implies Shimon Rokach was unrelated to Hasidism, but he came from a Sadigura family. Synagogue attribution (mixed Perushim+Hasidim, no named court) holds; Glatter is silent, so it does not override.",
        "founderCheck": "Problematic. The Huna Adler donor claim is supported by ynet (real, resolves). But \"ההקדש על שם ר' ישראל בן אליעזר כרמלוביץ'\" is a CONFLATION with the Jerusalem (Nahalat Shiva) \"קהל חסידים\", not the Tel Aviv building. No on-site rebbe/admor exists, consistent with a general shtibel. Atmag offers a competing founder (Shimon Rokach). Net: donor Adler plausible; Carmelovitch heqdesh as founder = false attribution, remove.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "Weakly supported / contested. ynet anchors construction to before Huna Adler's 1893 departure, supporting \"~1888–1893\". But atmag and go-arch/GuideStar give 1889 or 1890 for the buildings on this block. So \"~1888–1893\" is within range but imprecise — not fabricated. Neighborhood founding 1887 is correct.",
        "imageCheck": "No image/portrait was supplied or claimed; the research explicitly omits an admor portrait because no specific rebbe/court is tied to the site. There is no portrait to verify and no fabricated/gravestone-image risk. Correct editorial choice for a leaderless general \"קהל חסידים\" shtibel.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "CONFLATION/FABRICATION: psakdin Carmelovitch heqdesh case is a DIFFERENT synagogue (13 Yoel Solomon St, Nahalat Shiva, JERUSALEM; case 13955-08-10), not Neve Tzedek; wrongly placed in the founder field.",
          "ANACHRONISM: '1910 ... מראות הסולם established' — the name derives from Ashlag's 'הסולם' (1943–1953); cannot exist in 1910 (building itself ~1889).",
          "CONTESTED HOUSE NUMBER: קהל חסידים at רוקח 20 rests on ynet alone; atmag puts קהל חסידים א' at 18 and מראות הסולם at 20; go-arch/GuideStar put מראות הסולם at שמעון רוקח 18.",
          "OVERSTATED FOUNDER: Carmelovitch heqdesh founder claim unsupported; ynet supports DONOR Huna Adler; atmag credits Shimon Rokach.",
          "IMPRECISE YEAR: '~1888–1893' conflicts with 1889/1890 in other sources.",
          "MINOR: Shimon Rokach framed as non-Hasidic; he was from a Sadigura Hasidic family — still not Belz, so disambiguation holds, framing imprecise.",
