        "images": [],
        "gaps": "בכתובת שמרלינג 10 קיים בית כנסת (\"שערי תורה\"), אך הוא רשום כבית כנסת עדות המזרח ולא כשטיבל חסידי, ואינו משויך לאף שושלת חסידית. לכן שדה dynasty נותר ריק והדגל הוגדר not-a-synagogue במובן של \"אינו מוסד חסידי\" (קרי: לא שטיבל/חצר חסידית — אף שכן קיים שם מבנה בית כנסת מזרחי פעיל). לא נמצאה כל עדות במפתח גלטר או במקורות הפתוחים לקיומו של אדמו\"ר, חצר או שטיבל חסידי בכתובת זו לפני 1980. שם המפה (\"שמרלינג 10\") ככל הנראה שובץ בטעות בשכבת בתי הכנסת והשטיבלך החסידיים. מאחר שאין דמות אדמו\"ר, לא צורפה תמונת פורטרט. ביטחון נמוך לשיוך חסידי כלשהו — ולמעשה השיוך החסידי נשלל."
      },
      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "solid",
        "addressCheck": "CONFIRMED by Glatter (negative) and web (positive-but-non-Hasidic). The Glatter index contains NO entry for רחוב שמרלינג / Shmerling street at all — none of its documented Hasidic streets (Dizengoff, Feierberg, Rothschild, Achad Ha'am, Hillel HaZaken, Mohliver, Pinkas, HaAvoda, Rashi, Lilienblum) include Shmerling. So Glatter affirmatively does NOT support any Hasidic court/shtibel at this address, which is exactly what the anti-claim asserts. Independently, the official Tel Aviv Religious Council (rabanut.co.il) lists a real synagogue \"שערי תורה\" at שמרלינג 10 classified as עדות המזרח (Edot HaMizrach / Sephardi-Mizrahi), confirmed verbatim on the council's synagogue-search page. So a synagogue genuinely exists at the address, but it is a Mizrahi communal beit knesset, not a Hasidic shtibel or rebbe-home. The mapErrorFlag \"not-a-synagogue\" is mislabeled in spirit: a synagogue DOES exist there; it simply is not a Hasidic one. The intended meaning (\"not a Hasidic institution\") is correct, but the literal flag value is inaccurate and should be e.g. \"not-a-shtibel\" / \"non-hasidic-synagogue\".",
        "sourceQuality": "Good, load-bearing sources, all resolving except one. (1) rabanut.co.il religious-council search page — resolves and explicitly states שערי תורה, שמרלינג 10, עדות המזרח; authoritative for the synagogue's rite and directly supports the core finding. (2) Hebrew Wikipedia \"חיים שמואל שמרלינג\" — resolves, confirms 1826-1894, businessman/community activist (customs brokerage 1866, tobacco trade, co-founder of Jaffa Ashkenazi community), street named 1950, family's Chabad-mission origin to Hebron. (3) Chabadpedia — resolves, confirms businessman-not-rebbe and the Chabad-mission ancestry, BUT its dates are internally garbled (gives birth ~1826 yet \"died 1854 at age 69,\" impossible; Wikipedia's 1826-1894 is the consistent set). (4) The direct synagogue permalink /synagogue/שערי-תורה-2/ returned HTTP 404 (dead), but the same data is confirmed via the council's search-results page, so the substance still holds. The Glatter index serves as a strong negative control: silent on Shmerling, consistent with no Hasidic tie.",
        "dynastyCheck": "No dynasty claimed, correctly. The claim leaves dynasty empty and explicitly negates any Hasidic-court affiliation. Glatter confirms by omission (no Shmerling-street institution anywhere in the index). The web confirms the resident institution is Edot HaMizrach. The dynasty attribution (none) holds. Glatter and the research do not disagree — both point to NO Hasidic institution at this address.",
        "founderCheck": "No founder/rebbe claimed for the address, correctly. The claim's only named person is the STREET's namesake, Chaim Shmuel Shmerling, who is real (Wikipedia + Chabadpedia) and was explicitly a merchant/communal activist, NOT an admor or head of a Hasidic court. The claim's distinction — his FAMILY (grandfather R' Shimon Shmerling) came on a Chabad-rebbe mission to Hebron, while he himself was not a rebbe — is accurately supported by both Wikipedia and Chabadpedia. No conflation of the street namesake into a fake \"founder of a court\" occurs.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "No founding year is asserted for any Hasidic institution at the address, so there is no year to defend or refute — appropriate given the anti-claim. Ancillary dates are sound: street named 1950 (confirmed), Shmerling 1826-1894 (Wikipedia; Chabadpedia's conflicting \"died 1854/age 69\" is a garbled outlier to disregard). The claim that no shtibel/rebbe-home existed at the address \"before 1980\" is unfalsifiable from available sources but is not contradicted by anything found.",
        "imageCheck": "No images provided (images: []), which is appropriate and correct — there is no admor associated with this address, so no portrait should be fabricated. The claim explicitly and correctly explains the empty image field. Nothing to flag.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "mapErrorFlag value 'not-a-synagogue' is literally inaccurate: a real synagogue (שערי תורה) DOES exist at שמרלינג 10. The intended meaning is 'not a Hasidic shtibel/court'; the flag should be relabeled (e.g. 'non-hasidic-synagogue' or 'not-a-shtibel').",
          "Chabadpedia source gives internally inconsistent/garbled life dates ('died 1854 ... age 69' with birth ~1826); do not rely on it for dates — use Wikipedia's 1826-1894.",
          "Direct synagogue permalink (rabanut.co.il/synagogue/שערי-תורה-2/) is dead (HTTP 404); supporting evidence rests on the council search-results page instead — cite the working URL.",
          "Minor geographic conflation risk: the historical 'חצר שמרלינג' is associated with the Manshiya/Shabazi area (referenced near Feierberg 7), not necessarily the present-day Shmerling street in Neve Tzedek; story_he slightly blends the two."
        ],
        "corrections": "Core finding is CORRECT and well-supported: שמרלינג 10 hosts the שערי תורה synagogue, officially classified by the Tel Aviv Religious Council as עדות המזרח (Sephardi-Mizrahi), NOT a Hasidic shtibel or rebbe-home; the Glatter index has no entry for Shmerling street, corroborating the absence of any Hasidic court there; and the street's namesake, Chaim Shmuel Shmerling (1826-1894), was a merchant/communal activist (not a rebbe) whose family came to Hebron on a Chabad mission. Recommended corrections: (1) Change mapErrorFlag from 'not-a-synagogue' to 'non-hasidic-synagogue' / 'not-a-shtibel', since a synagogue does exist — it is simply Mizrahi, not Hasidic. (2) Replace the dead permalink source URL with the working council search page (rabanut.co.il/חיפוש-בתי-כנסת-בעיר/page/4/). (3) Drop reliance on Chabadpedia for life-dates and anchor to Wikipedia's 1826-1894. (4) Tighten story_he/dynastyBackground_he to avoid implying the original 'חצר שמרלינג' (Manshiya/Shabazi area, near Feierberg 7) is the same location as today's Shmerling street in Neve Tzedek. With these fixes the entry stands: this address was correctly excluded from the Hasidic map and should be removed from / re-tagged in the 'בתי כנסת ושטיבלך חסידיים' layer."
