        "addressCheck": "NO - Glatter does NOT support \"שדרות רוטשילד 12\". Glatter's Ozarov record (\"רבי יחיאל משה אפשטיין ... אוז'רוב ... ניו יורק ... 1953\", rebbe-home) carries NO street and NO house number and NO archivalRef. So Glatter neither states \"Rothschild\" nor \"12\" for Ozarov. The ONLY Rothschild entry in the entire Glatter index is a DIFFERENT institution: the Bohush rebbe (רבי יצחק פרידמן, origin Bucharest, 1951) at רוטשילד 112 (תיק 81120, מסמך 6146821, registered to Dr. Asher & Devora Hilman). That is a separate dynasty/person and must not be conflated with Ozarov. Meanwhile the open web converges on a COMPLETELY DIFFERENT number than \"12\": Hebrew Wikipedia (\"יהדות אורתודוקסית בתל אביב-יפו\") states the rebbe \"הקים בית כנסת בשדרות רוטשילד פינת רחוב לונץ, בסמוך לבית הספר ביל\\\"ו\" (built a synagogue at Rothschild corner of Luntz St, next to the Bilu school). The tel-aviv-pedia (tlv100.net) page titled \"בית מורי (דירת הרב אפשטיין)\" lives under the Masaryk/Orchestra-squares section with the URL slug \"sdr_126_128\" = Rothschild 126-128. Luntz/Bilu meet Rothschild at the NORTHEASTERN end (~Rothschild 122-128), the OPPOSITE end of the boulevard from No. 12 (the historic SW/Neve Tzedek end). Conclusion: \"Rothschild 12\" is contradicted, not merely unverified; the supportable address is Rothschild ~126-128 (corner Luntz). The claim's own gaps field actually spotted the Luntz lead and then wrongly dismissed it.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed-to-good. The five cited URLs are real and resolve: Hebrew Wikipedia (he.wikipedia \"משה יחיאל הלוי אפשטיין\"), Chabadpedia, MyTzadik, English Wikipedia, and Hebrew Wikipedia \"חסידות אוז'רוב\". They support the BIOGRAPHY well (dynasty, identity, USA 1926, aliyah 17 Tammuz 5713/1953, Israel Prize 1968, books Aish Dat & Be'er Moshe, Moetzet Gedolei HaTorah). BUT none of the cited sources support house number \"12\" - the biography page only says \"בתל אביב התגורר בשדרות רוטשילד עד סוף ימיו\" with no number, and Chabadpedia says only \"דרום תל אביב\". The decisive address evidence comes from sources the research did NOT cite but should have: he.wikipedia \"יהדות אורתודוקסית בתל אביב-יפו\" (Rothschild corner Luntz, near Bilu) and tlv100.net (slug 126-128). The research's claim that the Luntz lead \"could not be verified in any live source\" is FALSE - it is verifiable in live Hebrew Wikipedia.",
        "founderCheck": "REAL and correctly identified, but note the two-tier \"founder\" framing. Dynasty founder = רבי יהודה אריה לייב (לייבוש) אפשטיין (Ozarov). The Tel Aviv institution's founder = רבי משה יחיאל הלוי אפשטיין, the 5th Ozarov(-Chentshin) rebbe. He is a real, well-documented figure (Israel Prize 1968, author of Aish Dat and Be'er Moshe, president of Moetzet Gedolei HaTorah). He IS specifically tied to a Rothschild Blvd synagogue/home in Tel Aviv - so the person-to-place link is solid; only the house NUMBER is wrong.",
