        "addressCheck": "Glatter SUPPORTS the research's core correction, and the research is RIGHT to flag the map. Glatter places פיארברג 35 with VIZHNITZ (rebbe-home, Rabbi Eliezer Hager / \"אגודת דמשק אליעזר\", year 1944, archival refs את\"ב תיק 650130, מסמכים 7127528/7127291) — exactly matching the research. Glatter's Ozarov entry (\"רבי יחיאל משה אפשטיין ... אוז'רוב ... ניו יורק ... 1953\", type rebbe-home) carries NO street and NO number, so Glatter does NOT support Ozarov on Pierberg at all, and certainly not at #17. The corrected address logic holds: Pierberg = Vizhnitz #35 (not Ozarov), and the Ozarov site is Rothschild corner of Luntz. House number 17 on the map is unsupported by any source; #35 is the documented Pierberg address (Glatter only). Where Glatter and the map disagree, Glatter wins: the map's \"פיארברג 17 - אוז'רוב\" is a wrong-dynasty conflation. The research and Glatter AGREE; the only thing being overridden is the community map.",
        "sourceQuality": "Good. All 4 cited Hebrew Wikipedia URLs resolve and genuinely support their claims: (1) Ozarov dynasty article — confirms founding by R. Aryeh Leib, R. Moshe Yechiel Epstein as prominent leader, \"Esh Dat\"/\"Be'er Moshe\", center now Bnei Brak under R. Tanchum Beker (grandson). (2) Epstein bio — confirms name order Moshe Yechiel, b.1889/d.1971, aliyah 17 Tammuz 5713 (1953), settled on Rothschild Blvd until death, Israel Prize for Torah literature 5728/1968, honorary chairman of Moetzet Gedolei HaTorah. (3) Orthodox-Tel-Aviv article — explicitly states the Ozarov Rebbe \"הקים בית כנסת בשדרות רוטשילד פינת רחוב לונץ\" (verbatim support for the Luntz claim). (4) Eliezer Hager article — confirms Vizhnitz Admor, d.1946, aliyah 19 April 1944, founded Vizhnitz yeshiva in Tel Aviv. NOTE: Pierberg/35 itself appears ONLY in Glatter (with archive file numbers), not in open web — the research is transparent about this gap. No image was claimed (no free portrait found), so no image to fabricate.",
        "corrections": "1) FOUNDING DATES ERROR (founder background): Research says dynasty founded 1827, with R. Aryeh Leib \"rabbi of Ozarov from 1792, Admor from 1795.\" Hebrew Wikipedia says he became rabbi of Ozarov in תקע\"ב = 1812 and Admor in תקע\"ה = 1815 — NOT 1792/1795, and not 1827. Correct the founding to ~1815 (תקע\"ה) and drop the 1792/1795/1827 figures. This is the one substantive factual error. 2) The map label \"פיארברג 17 - אוז'רוב\" is a double error (wrong dynasty + wrong/unsupported number) — research correctly identifies this; keep mapErrorFlag \"wrong-dynasty\". 3) House number 17 is fabricated/unsupported in EVERY source — state plainly it appears in no source. 4) Name-order note is correct and useful: sources use \"משה יחיאל\"; Glatter inverts to \"יחיאל משה\" — a Glatter ordering quirk, harmless. 5) foundingYear field \"1953\" conflates the Ozarov Rebbe's aliyah year with a dynasty founding year — these are different things; the field is mislabeled but the underlying 1953 aliyah date is correct. 6) Minor: Hager's origin in Glatter is listed as טמשוואר (Timisoara); research says he came via escape from Vizhnitz — both compatible, no correction needed.",
        "dynastyCheck": "Dynasty attribution is the research's strongest point and is CORRECT. Pierberg is Vizhnitz, not Ozarov — confirmed by Glatter (explicit Pierberg 35 = Vizhnitz entry with archive refs) and consistent with open web (Eliezer Hager founded Vizhnitz yeshiva in TA; Ozarov Rebbe's TA site was Rothschild/Luntz). The map's Ozarov attribution to Pierberg is a genuine conflation of two separate courts. Verdict: research wins over the map; Glatter and research agree.",
        "founderCheck": "Founder is real. R. Aryeh Yehuda Leibush Epstein of Ozarov (student of the Chozeh of Lublin, son-in-law of R. Reuven of Dzharnovtsa) is the historical dynasty founder — confirmed by Wikipedia. The TA-relevant Admor, R. Moshe Yechiel Halevi Epstein, is also real and well-documented (Israel Prize 1968, Moetzet Gedolei HaTorah). BUT the founder is NOT tied to THIS address (Pierberg): neither founder has any documented connection to Pierberg. The Ozarov court's actual TA address is Rothschild corner of Luntz. So \"founder real\" = YES; \"founder tied to this address\" = NO — which is exactly the research's thesis.",
