        "founderCheck": "Founder is REAL and correctly described, but NOT tied to this address. R. Meir Yehiel Halevi Halshtok (1851-1928) founded Ostrovtza Hasidism, served as rabbi/av beit din of Ostrowiec in Poland for 39 years, and died (19 Adar 5688 / 11 Mar 1928) and was buried in Ostrowiec, Poland. He never operated in Tel Aviv. Wikipedia's only Tel Aviv link in his article is a disciple (R. Yitzhak Yedidya Frankel, later a Tel Aviv rabbi) — not the rebbe himself, and not a connection to any shtibel. Tying him to Merkaz Baalei Melakha 25 is an unsupported geographic conflation. Note: the founder's article and the Wikipedia text put his assumption of leadership after his teacher (R. Elimelech of Grodzisk) died (sources vary 1888/1892); irrelevant to the address question.",
