        "images": [],
        "gaps": "מפתח גלטר אינו כולל את אוסטרובצה כלל ואינו מזכיר את רחוב יוחנן הסנדלר; אין אסמכתא ארכיונית. במקורות הפתוחים (ויקיפדיה, מדריך רחובות, מאגר המועצה הדתית ת\"א) לא נמצאה כל ראיה לבית כנסת/שטיבל של חסידי אוסטרובצה ברחוב יוחנן הסנדלר 19 או בכל כתובת אחרת בתל אביב. שושלת ההנהגה של אוסטרובצה חוסלה בשואה (רבי יחזקאל הולשטוק ושבעת בניו נרצחו), ולא נמצא תיעוד להקמת חצר/מרכז אוסטרובצה בתל אביב. לפיכך הסטטוס הנוכחי, שנת הייסוד והקשר בין הכתובת לחסידות אינם מאומתים. ייתכן שמדובר במניין/שטיבל מקומי קטן בלתי מתועד, בשגיאת רישום במפה הקהילתית, או בבלבול עם מוסד אחר. לא צורפה תמונה: לא אותר דיוקן של אדמו\"ר אוסטרובצה בעל רישיון חופשי שדף הרישיון שלו נפתח ואומת, ועל פי הכללים מוטב להימנע מתמונה מאשר לנחש. נדרשים מקורות ארכיוניים/קהילתיים נוספים (למשל פנקסי המועצה הדתית, ספר \"אוסטרובצה – לזכרון ולעדות\" שיצא בתל אביב תשל\"ב) כדי לאשש או להפריך את הרישום."
      },
      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "addressCheck": "Glatter does NOT support the address. The Glatter index has zero entries for אוסטרובצה/Ostrovtza and zero for רחוב יוחנן הסנדלר; none of the 55 records mention Holshtok or this street, so it gives no street/house-number/year/archival ref for any Ostrovtza institution. Open web confirms the negative: the tlv-streets (Yon Bergman) page lists no synagogue at all and never mentions Ostrovtza; the artisans'-center (\"מרכז בעלי מלאכה\") neighborhood is correct. House number 19 is unsupported by any source. The ONLY synagogue repeatedly tied to this street in open web is a CHABAD \"Beit Moshe\"/Geulat Israel shul — strong evidence the map entry is a conflation/mislabel, not Ostrovtza. The research's \"unverifiable\" flag is correct; correctedAddress should stay empty since no Ostrovtza site in Tel Aviv could be located.",
        "sourceQuality": "Adequate for the dynasty, appropriately thin for the address (it is a negative finding). The three Wikipedia sources (מאיר יחיאל הולשטוק, יחזקאל הולשטוק, חסידות אורז'יטשוב) resolve and support the dynasty narrative. The tlv-streets and Religious-Council sources resolve and support the negative geographic finding. No fabricated URLs. No images attached — correct restraint. Weakness: the cited \"ספר אוסטרובצה – לזכרון ולעדות, ת\\\"א תשל\\\"ב\" in gaps is an unverified lead, not a confirmed source.",
        "dynastyCheck": "Real people, coherent attribution, but the background prose has errors. Confirmed: founder R. Meir Yechiel Halevi Holshtok (1851–1928); 40-year fast; ~39 years as Ostrovtza rabbi; son R. Yechezkel (b. 1886/7), disciple of the Chortkover rebbe David Moshe Friedman; Yechezkel and his seven children murdered in the Shoah; writings published as \"Kedoshei Yechezkel.\" But the dynasty has NO documented court/center in Tel Aviv post-Shoah, so tying it to a TA address is unsupported — the research correctly says so.",
        "founderCheck": "Founder is REAL but NOT tied to this address — the research states this correctly. R. Meir Yechiel Holshtok founded/led the court in Ostrowiec, Poland; no evidence he or any successor founded anything at Yohanan HaSandlar 19 or anywhere in Tel Aviv. Listing him as \"founder\" is only defensible because the research explicitly qualifies it (\"אין עדות שייסד מוסד בכתובת זו\").",
        "foundingYearCheck": "\"unknown\" is correct for the TA site (no evidence it ever existed). Separately, the background prose misstates the court's founding: it says he began as Ostrovtza rabbi in \"תרנ\\\"ב (1892)\", but sources give 1889 (תרמ\\\"ט) with a 39-year tenure ending 1928 — 1892 is incompatible with 39 years. Correct ≈ 1888/1889, not 1892.",
        "imageCheck": "No image attached, which is correct. No free-licensed verified portrait of an Ostrovtza rebbe was located; the research explicitly declined to guess. No gravestone or fabricated image URL present. Pass.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "DATE ERROR: background says Yechezkel was murdered in '1943'; 10 Tevet תש\"ג = 13 December 1942. Should be 1942.",
          "PLACE ERROR/CONFLATION: claim says he was shot 'near the synagogue wall IN OSTROVTZA'; sources place the execution near the synagogue wall in SANDOMIERZ, not Ostrowiec.",
          "FOUNDING-YEAR ERROR: 'החל בשנת תרנ\"ב (1892)' is inconsistent with the stated 39-year tenure to 1928; sources give 1889 (תרמ\"ט).",
          "UNSUPPORTED ADDRESS: 'יוחנן הסנדלר 19' and house number 19 have no support in Glatter or any open source.",
          "LIKELY CONFLATION: the only synagogue actually associated with Yohanan HaSandlar street in open web is Chabad 'Beit Moshe' — the Ostrovtza label is probably a map error/confusion.",
          "UNVERIFIED SOURCE LEAD: 'ספר אוסטרובצה – לזכרון ולעדות (ת\"א תשל\"ב)' cited in gaps is not independently confirmed."
        ],
        "corrections": "1) The central conclusion is CORRECT and should stand: no evidence of an Ostrovtza synagogue/shtibel at Yohanan HaSandlar 19 (or anywhere in Tel Aviv); status 'unverifiable'/likely map error or conflation. 2) Fix dynasty-background errors: (a) R. Meir Yechiel became Ostrovtza rabbi c.1889 (תרמ\\\"ט), NOT 1892 (תרנ\\\"ב) — only 1889 fits the 39-year tenure to 1928; (b) R. Yechezkel was murdered 10 Tevet תש\\\"ג = 13 December 1942, NOT 1943; (c) his execution was near the synagogue wall in SANDOMIERZ, not 'באוסטרובצה' — drop that phrase. 3) Add the probable real explanation for the pin: a CHABAD 'Beit Moshe'/Geulat Israel synagogue is the institution actually documented on Yohanan HaSandlar street; treat the Ostrovtza label as misidentification pending a community-register/Religious-Council source. 4) Keep founder, foundingYear, currentStatus, and image fields as-is — handled correctly. 5) Glatter and the research AGREE (no Ostrovtza, no Yohanan HaSandlar); Glatter is authoritative and confirms the negative — there is no Glatter-vs-research conflict to adjudicate."
      }
