      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "shaky",
        "addressCheck": "NOT supported. Glatter's Amshinov record (rebbe Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish, origin USA, year 1946, type rebbe-home) provides NO street, NO house number, and NO archival file reference — unlike the records Glatter DOES anchor (e.g. Modzhitz Dizengoff 36 w/ tik 1870360; Vizhnitz Fierberg 35 w/ tik 650130; Strelisk/Stratyn Hillel HaZaken 10 w/ tik 1200100; Bohush Rothschild 112). So even the authoritative index does not confirm \"המגיד 10\". No web source ties any Amshinov institution to HaMagid 10. The Tel Aviv religious council lists HaMagid street only as the \"Aharonson\" Ashkenazi synagogue (HaMagid 4, not 10, not Amshinov). The \"Ohel Yosef\" Amshinov shtibel (founded after R. Yosef Kalish's 1936 death) is real but has NO documented street. The address \"המגיד 10\" is unverifiable/unsupported by both Glatter and the open web.",
        "sourceQuality": "Sources are real and relevant but thin for the address question. Hebrew Wikipedia on R. Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish and on Hasidut Amshinov resolve and directly support the biography (USA late 1946; aliyah 1954; Bayit Vegan after Dec 1955) and the dynasty founding (1848, Yaakov David Kalish son of Yitzchak of Vorka). HaMichlol corroborates. The Tel Aviv religious council page is a legitimate independent check that, crucially, does NOT list Amshinov at HaMagid 10. No source — including Glatter — supplies an archival file number for this address, which is the core evidentiary gap.",
        "corrections": "(1) ADDRESS: Treat \"המגיד 10\" as unverified. Neither Glatter (no street/number/tik for the Amshinov record) nor any web source supports it. Do not assert an Amshinov institution at HaMagid 10. (2) YEAR/ANACHRONISM: The \"1946 Amshinov center in Tel Aviv led by R. Meir'l\" framing is anachronistic. In late 1946 the family moved to the USA; he only made aliyah in 1954 (after his father's death) and briefly lived in Tel Aviv before relocating to Jerusalem/Bayit Vegan after Dec 1955. Glatter's bare \"1946 / origin USA\" tag reflects the year he was abroad, NOT a Tel Aviv residence. Any genuine Tel Aviv presence of the rebbe was mid-1950s, not 1946. (3) The earlier, better-documented Amshinov footprint in Tel Aviv is the \"Ohel Yosef\" shtibel, established after R. Yosef Kalish's death on 3 Shevat 5696 (=1936) — but with no recorded street, so it cannot be pinned to HaMagid 10 either. (4) IMAGE: The lone portrait (קובץ:אמשינוב.jpg) is fair-use/copyright-protected, not free-licensed — correctly omitted; do not present it as a free portrait. (5) Center of gravity of Amshinov in Israel is Jerusalem (Bayit Vegan), not Tel Aviv.",
        "dynastyCheck": "CORRECT. Amshinov (אמשינוב, Mszczonów, Poland) is a real Polish Hasidic court, a branch of Vorka/Warka in the Przysucha-Vorka lineage. Founded 1848 by Rabbi Yaakov David Kalish, son of Rabbi Yitzchak of Vorka. Confirmed by Hebrew Wikipedia and HaMichlol. Dynasty attribution holds; matches Glatter's \"אמשינוב (Amshinov)\" record.",
        "founderCheck": "The named admor, Rabbi Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish (\"Reb Meir'l\"), is a real historical figure and a genuine Amshinov rebbe, matching Glatter exactly. BUT he is not specifically tied to the address HaMagid 10 by any source. He is also not the dynasty's \"founder\" — the dynasty was founded in 1848 by Yaakov David Kalish; the JSON's founder field correctly distinguishes these. Person real and dynasty-correct; address linkage unproven.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "The dynasty founding year 1848 is defensible and confirmed. The institution-at-this-address \"year 1946\" is NOT defensible as a Tel Aviv founding: in 1946 R. Meir'l left for the USA; he did not reside in Tel Aviv until ~1954. Glatter's \"1946 / USA\" entry is internally consistent with him being abroad, which actually contradicts a 1946 Tel Aviv rebbe-home. Anachronism flagged.",
        "imageCheck": "No image was attached, correctly. The only known portrait (Hebrew Wikipedia קובץ:אמשינוב.jpg) is tagged fair-use/copyright-protected, i.e. NOT free-licensed. Omission is the right call; no fabricated image URL present.",
