        "founderCheck": "Real and correctly identified, with one citation-internal discrepancy to flag. R. Yosef Kalish is genuine: rebbe who served in Ostrowa, moved to Otwock, died 3 Shevat תרצ\"ו/1936, buried in Warsaw — all confirmed by the toladot blog. He did NOT live in Tel Aviv; the shtibel was founded \"by his order\" and named after him posthumously — consistent across sources. The map's attribution of the founding to R. Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish is indeed wrong (he only reached Israel in 1954). DISCREPANCY: the research calls R. Yosef the \"third\" Amshinov rebbe; Hamichlol/Wikipedia support \"third\" (Yaakov David → Menachem → Yosef), but the cited toladot blog calls him the \"second\" (האדמו\"ר השני). The research sides with the encyclopedic sources, which is defensible, but the conflict among its own cited sources should be noted.",
