        "corrections": "1) Correct the map record: \"Zevulun 17 – Amshinov, R. Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish, 1946\" is not supportable. Zevulun street in Tel Aviv is documented at No. 25 for the BIALA court (R. Yechiel Yehoshua Rabinowitz, Siberia origin, arrived 1947). The Amshinov shtibel \"Ohel Yosef\" was founded by order of R. YOSEF Kalish (d. 1936), with no documented street address — its location at Zevulun (and especially No. 17) is unverified and likely a Biala/Amshinov conflation by the map editor. 2) Replace founder = Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir with founder = Yosef Kalish (3rd Amshinov rebbe per Wikipedia/Hamichlol; note one source says 2nd). 3) Replace foundingYear 1946 with \"pre-1936\"; treat Glatter's 1946 as the dynasty/USA timeline, not an address date. 4) Fix significance_he: R. Yerachmiel's \"Shem Olam\" yeshiva was in Holon, not Tel Aviv. 5) Reconsider mapErrorFlag — use \"wrong-address/wrong-rebbe/wrong-year\" rather than \"wrong-dynasty.\" 6) Where Glatter and open-web disagree on Zevulun: both actually AGREE — neither places Amshinov on Zevulun; the open web (Wikipedia) supplies the Biala/Zevulun-25 fact that Glatter only partially gives (Zevulun, no number). The research's reconciliation is correct."
