        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "addressCheck": "Glatter does NOT support any Hasidic institution at שלמה המלך 16, nor at שלמה המלך street at all. The authoritative Glatter index lists Hasidic addresses on Dizengoff 36, Ha'Avoda 15, Achad Ha'am, Pierberg 35, Rashi, Lilienblum, Hillel HaZaken 10, Rothschild 112, Mohliver 37, Pinkas — שלמה המלך appears nowhere, confirming the research. My independent web research found NO documented Hasidic court/shtibel/rebbe-home at number 16. IMPORTANT NUANCE the research missed: the Beit Chaviv twin building at שלמה המלך 31-33 (built 1939-40 for Rafael Chaviv) did at one historical point house \"a synagogue and a Beit HaChassidim of Gur (בית החסידים מגור)\" among many transient uses (also Beit HaChayal branch, soup kitchen, infirmary, leather factory, laundry) — per golden-lotus.co.il and project-tlv.info. This was a temporary use of a residential building, not a permanent Gur court, and it is at #31-33, NOT #16. So #16 itself remains unsupported, but the street is not entirely devoid of Hasidic-adjacent history.",
        "founderCheck": "No founder claimed, correctly. The research leaves dynasty/founder/rebbe/year blank because no concrete Hasidic institution could be tied to the address (the map record arrived with empty dynasty and empty note). There is no fabricated founder to flag.",
