        "corrections": "1) Core conclusion is CORRECT: no documented Hasidic shtibel/court/rebbe-home at שלמה המלך 16, neither in Glatter nor on the open web, and Glatter never lists שלמה המלך. The mapErrorFlag 'unverifiable' and 'low' confidence are appropriate. 2) ADD the missed nuance: the Beit Chaviv twin building at שלמה המלך 31-33 (built 1939-40 for Rafael Chaviv) did transiently house 'a synagogue and a Beit HaChassidim of Gur' (golden-lotus.co.il; project-tlv.info/buildings/shlomo-hamelech/31-33). This is the likely seed of any 'synagogue on Shlomo HaMelech' impression, but it is at #31-33, not #16, and was a temporary use, not a permanent Gur court. 3) Note the active Tel Aviv Gur synagogue is at Pierberg 17 (Nusach Ashkenaz, rabanut.co.il), reinforcing that Gur's documented address is elsewhere. 4) The secondary synagogue facts (בית שלמה = Yona HaNavi 27 Edot HaMizrach; מדרש שלמה = HaMaon 27 Florentine Ashkenaz; both not on Shlomo HaMelech, not Hasidic) are accurate. 5) Recommended revision: keep 'unverifiable' for #16 but soften the absolute phrasing 'אינה מזוהה ... כריכוז שטיבלך' to acknowledge the #31-33 Gur-Hasidim transient use elsewhere on the street. Sources: https://golden-lotus.co.il/haim-hotel/ ; https://project-tlv.info/buildings/shlomo-hamelech/31-33/ ; https://rabanut.co.il/synagogue/חסידי-גור/"
