        "addressCheck": "NOT SUPPORTED. Neither Glatter nor any open-web source ties \"החלוצים 43\" (HaChalutzim 43) to Amshinov or to Rabbi Meir'l Kalish. The authoritative Glatter index entry for Amshinov is bare: {dynasty: אמשינוב, rebbe: רבי ירחמיאל יהודא מאיר קאליש, origin: ארצות הברית, year: 1946, type: rebbe-home} with NO street, NO number, and NO archivalRef — unlike Modzhitz (דיזנגוף 36, file 1870360), Vizhnitz (פיארברג 35), Bohush (רוטשילד 112), etc. So Glatter neither confirms nor denies the street; it simply has no address data for Amshinov. My targeted web searches for \"החלוצים 43\" + synagogue/Hasidism and for Amshinov+החלוצים returned nothing linking the court to that address. The address is unverifiable, exactly as the research JSON concedes. Do NOT present HaChalutzim 43 as fact.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed but mostly legitimate. Hebrew Wikipedia (the Meir'l Kalish article and the Amshinov Hasidism article) and Chabadpedia resolve and substantively support the biography and dynasty. The Glatter article (Iyunim 36, Ben-Gurion Institute) is a real peer-reviewed academic source and is correctly cited; however the live PDF at in.bgu.ac.il repeatedly refused direct fetches (ECONNREFUSED — it blocks non-browser clients), so I relied on the provided authoritative Glatter index plus search snippets rather than reading the PDF firsthand. The four cited source URLs are all real and topically correct. No fabricated URLs detected.",
        "corrections": "1) ADDRESS: Strip or hard-flag \"החלוצים 43\". It has zero support in Glatter (no street/number) and zero open-web corroboration. Best honest statement: address unverified/unknown; do not assert it. 2) YEAR/PRESENCE: The \"1946\" is real in Glatter but means the rebbe's recorded location was the USA in 1946, NOT a Tel Aviv institution founded in 1946. Per Wikipedia, the family emigrated to the USA in late 1946 and Meir'l reached Eretz Yisrael only in 1954 (after his father's death). His Tel Aviv stay was a brief first stop in 1954–1955 before Holon (Shem Olam yeshiva) and then Jerusalem/Bayit Vegan (permanent center, from end of 1955). So a \"1946 Tel Aviv rebbe-home\" framing is an anachronism/conflation — correct the founding/presence year for Tel Aviv to ~1954, brief and transitional. 3) DYNASTY/FOUNDER of the SITE vs DYNASTY founder: Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish is correctly the Amshinov rebbe in Israel, but he is NOT the dynasty's founder (that is Yaakov David Kalish, 1848, Mszczonów); the JSON already states this correctly as \"4th rebbe\" — keep that distinction clear. 4) CONFLATION RISK: The older Tel Aviv Amshinov shtibel \"אוהל יוסף\" (established after R. Yosef Kalish's death, 1936) is a DIFFERENT institution, not at HaChalutzim 43 and not R. Meir'l's; today an \"Ohel Yosef\" synagogue exists on Sderot HaChayil — do not merge these. 5) IMAGE: Correct to include none. No verified free-licensed PORTRAIT of Meir'l Kalish exists on Commons; available images are of his father Shimon Shalom or unidentified Amshinov rebbes — do not substitute the father's portrait.",
        "dynastyCheck": "HOLDS. Amshinov (אמשינוב/Mszczonów) is a Polish Hasidic court, a branch of Vorka (Warka), founded mid-19th c. (1848) by Rabbi Yaakov David Kalish, son of R. Yitzhak of Vorka. Confirmed by Hebrew Wikipedia. The rebbe attribution (R. Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish = Amshinov in Israel) is correct and matches Glatter's Amshinov entry exactly.",
        "founderCheck": "REAL person, correctly identified. Rabbi Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish (\"Rabbi Meir'l\"), b. 22 Mar 1905 Pshischa, son of R. Shimon Shalom Kalish, d. 27 May 1976 Jerusalem (buried Mount of Olives). He is the Amshinov rebbe who established the court's Israel center (Bayit Vegan). Caveat: he is the 4th-generation rebbe, NOT the dynasty founder, and his tie to a SPECIFIC Tel Aviv address is unproven — Glatter records him under origin \"USA, 1946,\" and his actual Tel Aviv residence was a brief 1954–55 way-station.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "DEFENSIBLE ONLY AS A GLATTER DATA POINT, NOT AS A TEL AVIV FOUNDING. Glatter lists 1946, but Wikipedia shows 1946 = the family's move to the USA, and Meir'l reached Israel/Tel Aviv only in 1954. So \"founded in Tel Aviv 1946\" is an anachronism. Corrected: any Tel Aviv presence of R. Meir'l dates to ~1954 and was transitional; the permanent Amshinov center is Jerusalem/Bayit Vegan from late 1955.",
        "imageCheck": "No image included, which is correct. No verified free-licensed PORTRAIT of R. Yerachmiel Yehuda Meir Kalish exists; Wikimedia Commons holdings are of his father R. Shimon Shalom Kalish or unidentified/later Amshinov figures. Including the father's image as if it were the founder would be a misattribution — correctly avoided.",
