        "addressCheck": "Glatter does NOT support an \"Ashlag\" institution at Florentin 44 — or at any Florentin address. Confirmed against the supplied Glatter index and corroborated on the open web: the ONLY \"Ashlag\"-bearing entry in Glatter is \"סטרטין־אשלג (Stratyn-Ashlag)\" — Rabbi Yehuda Zvi Brandwein, a SHTIBEL at הלל הזקן 10 (Hillel HaZaken 10), year 1944, with archival refs את\"ב תיק 1200100, מסמכים 9115461/9115389. Florentin street appears nowhere in Glatter. The research JSON's own correctedAddress (Hillel HaZaken 10) is the right call IF the intended court is Stratyn-Ashlag. Independent web check: Florentin 44 resolves to the Eltan Group residential preservation building (14 apartments over one commercial floor, architect Adam Cohen, TAMA project) — confirmed, no synagogue. A nearby synagogue exists around Florentin 43 (\"אהבת חסד\" Ashkenazi), but it is NOT named Ashlag and is a different address. So: address↔dynasty pairing is unsupported; corrected address (Hillel HaZaken 10) is Glatter-backed.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed but the research is honestly sourced and self-skeptical. The four cited URLs are all real and resolve: he.wikipedia \"חסידות אשלג\", HaMichlol \"חסידות אשלג\", he.wikipedia \"אברהם מרדכי גוטליב\", and the Eltan Group Florentin 44 page (verified — confirms residential preservation building, no synagogue). These genuinely support the BACKGROUND claims (Ashlag dynasty centered in Bnei Brak/Jerusalem; Florentin 44 = apartments). They do NOT support — and the JSON never claims they support — an Ashlag institution at Florentin 44. The authoritative Glatter PDF (in.bgu.ac.il/bgi/iyunim/36) is real and surfaced in search, though direct fetch was refused (ECONNREFUSED); its Stratyn-Ashlag/Hillel HaZaken 10 content is corroborated by the supplied index and HaMichlol/Wikipedia. No fabricated URLs. images[] is empty, so no fake/gravestone portrait was inserted — appropriately, since no rebbe can be tied to this address.",
