        "dynastyCheck": "\"Ashlag\" as a court name is real (kabbalistic-Hasidic courts descending from R. Yehuda Leib Ashlag, Baal HaSulam, 1885-1954, \"Baal HaSulam,\" author of the Sulam commentary on the Zohar). But it is NOT attested at Florentin 44. In Glatter, \"Ashlag\" exists only fused as \"Stratyn-Ashlag\" via Brandwein. The research correctly separates pure-Ashlag (Bnei Brak/Jerusalem/Kiryat Ye'arim/Beitar/Beit Shemesh) from Stratyn-Ashlag (Hillel HaZaken 10). Dynasty attribution to THIS address fails.",
