        "dynastyCheck": "CONFIRMED. Boyan is a branch of the Ruzhin dynasty, founded in Boiany (Bukovina) by Rabbi Yitzchak Friedman (d. 1917), grandson of Rabbi Israel of Ruzhin. After his death his sons became rebbes and dispersed; Rabbi Israel Friedman was the SECOND son and led the Leipzig branch (\"בנו השני, רבי ישראל כיהן בלייפציג שבגרמניה\"). Hebrew Wikipedia's Boyan article confirms all of this. Dynasty attribution is solid.",
        "founderCheck": "CONFIRMED and real, specifically tied to the institution (a beit midrash on Yavne St, Tel Aviv). Rabbi Israel Friedman (1878–1951), Boyaner Rebbe of Leipzig, fled Nazis to Switzerland 1939, immigrated to Eretz Israel, settled in Tel Aviv, opened a beit midrash on Yavne Street, traveled to Meron on Lag BaOmer for the family lighting tradition, died 1 Sept 1951 (א' דר\\\"ח אלול תשי\\\"א), buried in the Old Cemetery in Safed. All verified. He is tied to THIS street specifically — not merely the dynasty elsewhere — though the exact building number is not pinned.",
