      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "founderCheck": "CONFIRMED REAL and correctly identified. Rabbi Israel Friedman of Boyan-Leipzig (1878-1951): son of Rabbi Yitzhak Friedman (\"Pachad Yitzhak\"), first Admor of Boyan; established his court in Leipzig (hence \"Boyan-Leipzig\"), fled the Nazis to Switzerland in 1939, immigrated to Tel Aviv, opened a beit midrash, buried in the old cemetery in Safed. Hebrew Wikipedia and mytzadik confirm. CONFLATION RISK CHECKED: Glatter contains TWO different rebbes named \"רבי ישראל פרידמן\" — one from Hoesiatin/Husiatyn (origin Vienna, 1937) and one from Boyan-Leipzig (origin Boyan, 1940). The research correctly anchored to the Boyan-Leipzig entry and did not conflate them. Founder is real and correctly tied to this dynasty; NOT tied to the Montefiore address by any source.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "DEFENSIBLE. Glatter gives 1940 for Boyan-Leipzig (rebbe-home), cited correctly. Independent sources confirm he fled in 1939, spent months in Switzerland, then arrived in Mandatory Palestine — consistent with a ~1940 establishment. No anachronism. The \"(לפי גלאטר; עלה ארצה לאחר 1939)\" qualifier is honest.",
        "dynastyCheck": "CONFIRMED. Boyan is a branch of the Ruzhin dynasty, founded by Rabbi Yitzhak Friedman, grandson of Israel of Ruzhin, son of Avraham Yaakov of Sadigura. Town of Boyan near Chernovtsy in Bukovina. Branches accurate per Hebrew Wikipedia (Chernovtsy, Leipzig, Lvov/Lemberg, Vienna-NY). Today centered in Jerusalem with large concentration in Beitar Illit. Minor imprecision: research's \"Boyan-Krakow\" should be Lvov/Lemberg, not Krakow — does not affect core claim.",
        "addressCheck": "Map address \"Montefiore 7\" is NOT supported by ANY source and is correctly flagged as wrong. Glatter provides NO street or house number for Boyan-Leipzig (no archival file reference — unlike Modzhitz/Dizengoff 36, Munkacs/HaAvoda 15, Vizhnitz/Fierberg 35, which DO have At\"b file numbers); it is simply silent on the address. Multiple independent sources (Hebrew Wikipedia, mytzadik, Michlol/Chabadpedia) place the beit midrash on YAVNE Street. project-tlv confirms Montefiore 7 was the Wolkowiski-Feingold \"Montefiore Real School\" building, later restaurants, now a hotel project — never a synagogue/shtibel. Corrected address (Yavne street, no verified house number) is the best-supported conclusion; the research's caution about the unverified house number is correct.",
        "imageCheck": "No image attached (images array empty) — correct. The research states no free-licensed Wikimedia Commons portrait exists. mytzadik has a labeled photo plus a gravestone image but is not free-licensed, so properly excluded. No fabricated or gravestone image passed off as a portrait. Clean.",
        "sourceQuality": "Good and honest. All 5 cited URLs resolve and support their attributed claims: (1) Hebrew Wikipedia explicitly says beit midrash on Yavne Street, confirms 1878-1951, father, Leipzig court, Safed burial. (2) Wikipedia Boyan confirms lineage. (3) mytzadik confirms identity and TA beit midrash (no street named). (4) project-tlv confirms Montefiore 7 was a school then restaurants then hotel project, NEVER a synagogue. (5) Michlol corroborates Wikipedia. The research also investigated and correctly DEBUNKED golden-lotus.co.il's \"Bet Friedman, Yavne 7\" as a secular Yosef Dov Friedman building unrelated to the Admor — a real conflation trap it avoided.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "Map address 'Montefiore 7' is unsupported by every source and contradicted by Yavne street; correctly flagged, but it is really a wrong-STREET error, not merely a wrong number.",
          "Glatter provides NO street/number/archival reference for Boyan-Leipzig; the address rests entirely on open-web (Wikipedia/Michlol/mytzadik), not Glatter. The research states this correctly.",
          "Minor: dynastyBackground lists 'Boyan-Krakow'; the actual third branch was Lvov/Lemberg, not Krakow.",
          "golden-lotus 'Yavne 7' is a SECULAR Yosef Dov Friedman residence, NOT the Admor's beit midrash; the Friedman+Yavne coincidence must not be treated as confirming Yavne 7 as the shtibel address. Research correctly avoided this.",
          "currentStatus 'closed' is defensible: no successor to the Leipzig branch and the beit midrash did not long survive him."
        ],
        "corrections": "1) Replace \"Montefiore 7\" with \"Yavne Street, Tel Aviv\" (no verified house number). The mapErrorFlag is better characterized as wrong-STREET than wrong-number: Montefiore 7 was the Montefiore Real School building (later restaurants, now an Isrotel hotel project), never a synagogue. 2) Do NOT adopt \"Yavne 7\": golden-lotus.co.il's \"Bet Friedman, Yavne 7\" is a secular Yosef Dov Friedman building unrelated to the Admor. 3) State explicitly that Glatter does NOT corroborate any address for Boyan-Leipzig (no archival file number for this entry); the Yavne attribution rests solely on Hebrew Wikipedia/Michlol/mytzadik. 4) Minor: the dynasty's third branch is Lvov/Lemberg, not Krakow. 5) Confidence \"medium\" is appropriate: rebbe identity, dynasty, and 1940 are solid; exact house number is genuinely unverified. Where Glatter and the research meet on the address they do not contradict — Glatter is silent, so the open-web Yavne attribution stands as best available and Montefiore 7 is the clear map error."
      }
