        "founderCheck": "CONFIRMED and specifically tied to this address. R. Yechiel Yehoshua Rabinowitz (1900-1982), author of \"Chelkat Yehoshua,\" Admor of Biala, member of the Council of Torah Sages of Agudath Israel, is a real historical figure. He is tied to Zevulun 25 by his own 1947 letter (\"my apartment on Zevulun Street 25\") -- this is THIS founder at THIS address, not the dynasty merely existing elsewhere. He is buried on the Mount of Olives (Warsaw section), died 21 Shevat 5742/1982.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "CLAIM (1947) is CORRECT; Glatter (1946) is the one that errs here. The primary letter dated 1.9.1947 announcing entry into the Zevulun 25 apartment, plus Wikipedia/HaMichlol/zadikim all giving Lag BaOmer תש\"ז = 1947 for his aliyah and establishment of the beit midrash, beat Glatter's 1946. Glatter's 1946 most likely reflects a generalized arrival-in-country estimate; the dwelling/beit midrash at this address is unambiguously 1947. Where Glatter and the research disagree on the year, the RESEARCH is correct. Defensible.",
        "dynastyCheck": "SOLID. Biala is a Polish Hasidic dynasty from Biala Podlaska, a branch of the Peshischa school descending from the \"Holy Jew\" of Peshischa via his son R. Yerachmiel (confirmed: Holy Jew -> R. Yerachmiel of Peshischa -> R. Natan David of Shidlovtsa -> founder R. Yitzchak Yaakov Rabinowitz). The dual Biala-Ozarov tie is REAL and documented: he grew up in the home of his maternal grandfather the Ozarov rebbe (Arieh Leib II), and the Ozarov Wikipedia article confirms he served as Admor for Ozarov hasidim in Israel at the request of R. Moshe Yechiel (Epstein) during the latter's years in the USA. Ozarov founder = R. Arieh Leib, disciple of the Chozeh of Lublin, center today in Bnei Brak -- all confirmed. No conflation; the dual attribution is genuine and unusual, as the JSON claims.",
