        "founderCheck": "Real, but role nuance. רבי מנחם נחום עפשטיין (1846–1918) is a real, documented founder of the Kobrin-Bialystok court (Wikipedia confirms dates and the 1896 Bialystok relocation). He is NOT tied to Lilienblum 4 — he never reached Tel Aviv (died 1918 in Europe). The Tel Aviv figure רבי שמואל אהרן שצדרוביצקי (1907–1978) is also real and did settle in Tel Aviv in 1943, but his own Wikipedia page describes him as the SON of the Kobrin-Bialystok admor and as a senior Agudat Yisrael activist / deputy chair of the Tel Aviv religious council — NOT explicitly as a serving rebbe. Neither founder is tied to THIS address; only the dynasty-elsewhere connection holds.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "\"unknown\" is the correct and defensible answer. No source dates a shtibel at Lilienblum 4. The 1943 date (Shmuel Aharon's arrival in Palestine) is real and well-sourced but is the person's arrival, not the founding of any institution at that address. The JSON handles this correctly by labeling founding year unknown and separating it from the 1943 biographical fact.",
