        "sourceQuality": "Good and mostly verifiable. Golden Lotus (golden-lotus.co.il/beit-habad) resolves and fully supports the family narrative: three brothers Ben-Zion/Yehoshua-Zeev/Yaakov, roots in Mir (Minsk district), oil trade in Odessa, ~1907 factory, Rabbi Kook's hechsher, not expelled in WWI due to Ottoman army oil needs, Dizengoff naming the alley. Hebrew Wikipedia \"אחוה (מותג)\" resolves and confirms Achdut Ltd. founded 1929 at Simtat Beit Habad (180 sqm), street named by Dizengoff — though it does NOT itself name the Breslav family or \"Derech Yafo,\" so the family attribution rests on Golden Lotus alone. The boutik.co.il real-estate page resolves and confirms Derech Yafo 13 / Simtat Beit Habad 2-4: built 1911, textile shops, award-winning 2016 conservation. The breslevcity source confirms modern Breslov (Heichal Hakodesh) is at Hashoshanim 9 / Kikar Shalom, NOT this address. The project-tlv page is thin (location/photos only, no history). No image sources to assess — images array is empty (appropriately, since no portrait exists for a misattributed institution).",
