        "addressCheck": "NOT SUPPORTED. Neither Glatter nor the open web supports \"יצחק אלחנן 27\" as a Breslov shtibel. The Glatter index entry for Breslov is bare: {\"dynasty\":\"ברסלב\",\"type\":\"shtibel\",\"quote\":\"מרכזים חסידיים אחרים בעיר היו עבור החסידויות האלה: ... ברסלב ...\"} — it has NO rebbe, NO street, NO house number, and NO archival file reference (unlike the genuinely documented entries such as מונקאטש/העבודה 15 תיק 210150, סטרטין/הלל הזקן 10 תיק 1200100, ללוב/מוהליבר 37 תיק 1320370). So Glatter provides zero house-number authority here and cannot OVERRIDE anything toward \"27.\" Web searches for \"יצחק אלחנן 27\" + Breslov returned nothing; the only synagogue surfaced near that number was Sephardic \"צעירי המזרח\" at a different street (\"נווה צדק 27\"), not Breslov. The \"27\" appears fabricated/unverifiable — it is a precise house number with no source. The research JSON itself rates this address \"unverifiable / low confidence,\" which is appropriate; the failure is that a falsely-precise address (\"27\") was generated at all.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed. The four cited URLs all resolve and are real, but they do NOT support the headline claim — they only support the dynasty background and the negative finding. (1) he.wikipedia \"חסידות ברסלב\" resolves and confirms founder, no living rebbe since 1810, R. Natan, Uman — but says nothing about יצחק אלחנן 27 (correctly cited only for background). (2) rabanut.co.il religious-council directory — generic, no entry for this address. (3) project-tlv.info synagogue list resolves but does NOT list a Breslov shtibel at יצחק אלחנן 27, AND does NOT corroborate the JSON's own side-claim of a \"תורה ותפילה\" synagogue at יצחק אלחנן 15 — that nearby-synagogue detail is itself unsupported by the cited source. (4) breslevcity.co.il \"היכל הקודש\" resolves and places that institution at רחוב הבושם 9, כפר שלום (south TLV) — confirming it is unrelated to the disputed address. No archival/primary source ties Breslov to number 27.",
        "corrections": "1) ADDRESS: Drop the precise \"יצחק אלחנן 27.\" No source (Glatter or web) supports a house number; Glatter lists Breslov only as an unlocated \"other center.\" State address as UNKNOWN, not 27. 2) GLATTER OVERRIDE: The prompt's premise that Glatter \"may override web geographic reasoning with exact house numbers\" does NOT apply here — the Breslov entry has no street/number/file, so it cannot validate \"27.\" 3) MODERN-COMMUNITY ERROR: The JSON twice mislocates קהילת \"שיר חדש.\" Its synagogue/beit midrash is on שדרת הר ציון, Tel Aviv; only the distribution center was at ארלוזורוב 86. The JSON's \"ברחוב ארלוזורוב בצפון העיר\" is wrong on two counts — it conflates the distribution center with the community's seat, and Arlozorov is central, not \"north.\" 4) FOUNDER/DYNASTY: Correct and well-supported — R. Nachman of Breslov (1772–1810), great-grandson of the Baal Shem Tov; no living rebbe since 1810 (\"dead Hasidim\"); R. Natan Sternharz spread the teachings; Uman gathering. Keep. 5) FOUNDING YEAR: \"unknown\" is the honest and correct value; do not invent one. 6) IMAGE: Correct to omit. R. Nachman pre-dates photography and has no authentic portrait; the only circulating image is a disputed dream-vision painting (attributed to A.C. Biton) that Breslov rabbis reject as baseless — so an empty images[] is right, and attaching any \"portrait\" would be a fabrication. 7) NET: This is essentially a NON-INSTITUTION — a real dynasty pinned to a fabricated-precision address. Recommend reclassifying as \"dynasty present in TLV, specific shtibel location unknown\" rather than an entry keyed to יצחק אלחנן 27.",
        "dynastyCheck": "SOLID. Breslov founder, lineage (great-grandson of the Baal Shem Tov), the \"no living rebbe / dead Hasidim\" doctrine since 1810, R. Natan Sternharz's editing/printing of ליקוטי מוהר\"ן, and the Uman Rosh Hashana ingathering are all confirmed by he.wikipedia \"חסידות ברסלב.\" Glatter independently lists Breslov as a TLV \"other center\" (shtibel), so the dynasty's mere presence in Tel Aviv is plausible. The dynasty attribution itself is not the problem — the address pinning is.",
        "founderCheck": "SOLID. רבי נחמן מברסלב (1772–1810) is a real historical figure, founder of Breslov, great-grandson of the Baal Shem Tov — confirmed by Wikipedia. BUT he is tied here only to the DYNASTY, never to THIS address: he died in Uman in 1810, more than a century before any Tel Aviv institution could exist, and the JSON correctly does not claim he personally founded the יצחק אלחנן 27 shtibel. There is no named local rebbe/founder for the specific shtibel (consistent with Breslov having no living rebbe). So \"founder real\" = yes; \"founder specifically tied to this address\" = no, and correctly so.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "\"unknown\" — defensible and honest. No source gives a founding year for a Breslov presence at this address (or any TLV address). Glatter assigns years to documented rebbe-homes/shtibels but gives NONE for Breslov. Inventing a year would be fabrication; leaving it unknown is correct.",
        "imageCheck": "CORRECT to have no image. R. Nachman (d. 1810) predates photography and left no authentic portrait; halachic/Breslov tradition holds no true likeness exists, and the one circulating \"portrait\" is a disputed dream-vision painting that Breslov rabbis publicly reject as baseless (some calling reliance on it idolatrous). An empty images[] array is the right call; any attached \"portrait of the rebbe\" would be a fabricated/inauthentic image.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
