        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "addressCheck": "PARTIALLY supported, with an important caveat. Glatter does NOT support any street/house number for Gur at all — the research JSON itself concedes this (\"גלאטר אינו נוקב רחוב/מספר בית לגור\"). Glatter's Gur entry is a dispersed network (\"16 בתי תפילה\" in early תש\"ך/1960, archival ref אעת\"א חטיבה 8 מיכל 2331 תיק 30-1960-2), type beit-midrash, rebbe Yisrael Alter (Jerusalem), local rep Yehuda Meir Abramovitz — confirmed, but address-agnostic. The corrected address \"Bar Ilan 4\" is supported instead by OPEN-WEB sources: the Tel Aviv Religious Council (rabanut.co.il) lists \"בית יעקב ואוהל רבקה - חסידי גור\" at בר אילן 4, Nusach Ashkenaz, active — verified live. Hebrew Wikipedia confirms the surviving TA Gur community is split between \"שטייבל בר-אילן ופיארברג.\" The map's \"ברזילי 4\" is unsupported: project-tlv.info confirms Brazilai is a residential/development street in Gan HaChashmal with no religious institution. So the \"Bar Ilan 4 not Brazilai\" correction is well-reasoned and defensible, but rests on phonetic similarity + council listing + Wikipedia, NOT on Glatter. No house-number-level archival proof for Bar Ilan 4 exists. Where Glatter and the research \"disagree\" they actually don't — Glatter is simply silent on address, so it neither confirms nor refutes Bar Ilan 4; it does refute any claim that the academic source pins Gur to a specific number.",
        "sourceQuality": "Good. Rabanut.co.il (TA Religious Council) is an authoritative live primary source confirming name/address/affiliation/Nusach at Bar Ilan 4. Hebrew Wikipedia corroborates the bar-ilan + פיארברג shtibels and Yisrael Alter (d.1977). English Wikipedia confirms Yisrael Alter served 1948-1977, Jerusalem-based, buried on Mount of Olives. The Glatter PDF (in.bgu.ac.il / kotar.cet.ac.il) is a real peer-reviewed academic article (\"אדמו״רים ברחובות תל אביב 1940-1965\", Iyunim vol. 36) and its abstract/snippets confirm Gur-as-largest-core and Abramovitz's role; full-text fetch was blocked (ECONNREFUSED / abstract-only paywall) so the exact 16-prayer-houses quote and archival file number could not be byte-verified, but the search snippet reproduced \"16 בתי תפילה\" verbatim. Wikimedia image file resolves and is genuine.",
        "dynastyCheck": "Correct. Gur (גור / Góra Kalwaria) founded 19th c. by Yitzchak Meir Alter (Chiddushei HaRim), continued by Sfas Emes and Imrei Emes — all accurate. Gur was indeed the largest Hasidic presence in Tel Aviv. Dynasty attribution to the Bar Ilan 4 synagogue is explicitly confirmed by the synagogue's own name and the Religious Council listing (\"חסידי גור\").",
        "founderCheck": "Defensible and honestly framed. The JSON does NOT claim an individual \"founder\" of this shtibel — correctly so. It names Yisrael Alter (\"Beit Yisrael\") as the era's Rebbe (Jerusalem-based, NOT founder of this specific synagogue) and Yehuda Meir Abramovitz as the local representative. Both are real and verified: Yisrael Alter (1895-1977, Rebbe 1948-1977, Jerusalem) and Abramovitz (1914-2007, Agudat Israel/Gur figure, Knesset member, tied to Gur Tel Aviv in Glatter). No fabricated founder. Good practice that the JSON warns against attributing the global Gur court (Jerusalem, Beit Yisrael) to this local shtibel.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "Honestly reported as unknown — no fabrication. The JSON does not invent a founding year for Bar Ilan 4; it only notes the broader Gur TA community dates to the 1919-1929 immigration wave, which is historically plausible. No anachronism: Yisrael Alter (Rebbe 1948-1977) is correctly placed as the Rebbe of the \"documented period\" (Glatter covers 1940-1965 / the 1960 figure). No defensible specific year exists for the building, and none was asserted.",
        "imageCheck": "REAL and appropriate. File:Beis_Yisroel.jpg on Wikimedia Commons is a genuine CC BY-SA 4.0 portrait photograph (not a gravestone, not a fabricated URL — it resolves). Depicts Yisrael Alter (the Beit Yisrael, Rebbe of Gur) alongside the Tolna Rebbe (Yitzchak Menachem Weinberg) and R. Yaakov Weil. Caption is accurate. One minor note: it is a group photo, not a solo portrait, but Alter is the subject and correctly identified.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "Address 'Bar Ilan 4' is NOT supported by Glatter (the academic index gives no street/number for Gur) — it is supported only by the open-web Religious Council listing + Wikipedia + phonetic reasoning. The JSON's 'high confidence' rests on inference, not archival proof.",
          "The Brazilai→Bar Ilan correction is a reasonable hypothesis but unproven: no source documents a Gur institution being intended at Brazilai, so it cannot be 100% excluded that the map plotted a different/erroneous point. JSON acknowledges this in 'gaps'.",
          "Glatter full-text (16 בתי תפילה quote + archival file אעת\"א מיכל 2331 תיק 30-1960-2) could not be byte-verified due to PDF fetch failure; relies on search-snippet reproduction. Treat the exact file number as unconfirmed though plausible.",
