        ],
        "corrections": "1) The map pin 'Gur synagogue at Yehuda Halevi 85' should be removed or relabeled as a location error — there is no Gur institution there; it is the Beit Silon commercial building. 2) Use the verified Gur addresses instead: Fiarbarg (פיירברג) 17 (per rabanut.co.il and the Religious Council), Bar-Ilan, Echad Ha'am, and Kishon 33 (per Hebrew Wikipedia). 3) Keep the founder/rebbe distinction explicit: founder = Yitzchak Meir Alter (Chiddushei HaRim, d. 1866); 1960 rebbe = Yisrael Alter (Beis Yisroel, 1948–1977), based in Jerusalem, NOT Tel Aviv. 4) Do not attach File:GerrerRebbe.JPG to a 1960 institution — it is the 2006 rebbe; either omit (as done) or source a period-appropriate image of Yisrael Alter. 5) Minor: present the synagogue count as '7 by 1949, 16 prayer houses by 1960' to harmonize Wikipedia and Glatter rather than citing only one. Overall the research is honest, correctly cautious, and its core conclusion (address is a map error; dynasty/founder/rebbe facts are sound) is well-supported."
