        "overallVerdict": "shaky",
        "addressCheck": "PARTIALLY UNSUPPORTED. Street (\"Lilienblum\") is supported; the house number \"16\" is NOT supported by Glatter and is conflated. Glatter's Lilienblum entry names Eliezer Hager (rebbe-home + High Holidays in adjacent hall) with NO house number and NO archival reference. Independent web sources (yeshiva.org.il / hamichlol / Wikipedia mirrors) tie \"Lilienblum 16\" specifically to the brother/successor רבי חיים מאיר הגר (Imrei Chaim), who resided there until תשי\"א/1951 before moving to Bnei Brak — NOT to Eliezer Hager. The research grafts Chaim Meir's house number \"16\" onto Eliezer Hager's numberless Glatter entry. Note Glatter's only Vizhnitz rebbe-home WITH a hard archival cite + house number is a DIFFERENT site: Pierberg 35 (פיארברג 35, תיק 650130), registered to Agudat Damesek Eliezer. So Glatter supports the street but neither confirms nor supplies \"16\" for Eliezer's Lilienblum residence.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed. The image (Damesekeliezer.JPG) is a genuine, free-licensed (PD-Israel) PORTRAIT of the correct subject — verified, solid. Wikipedia bio (אליעזר הגר דמשק אליעזר) resolves and supports: born 1891, aliyah 26 Nisan תש\"ד = 19 Apr 1944, died ב' אלול תש\"ו = 2 Aug 1946, buried Mount of Olives, no children, succeeded by brother Chaim Meir, founded Vizhnitz yeshiva in Tel Aviv — but does NOT mention Lilienblum. ישיבת בית ישראל ודמשק אליעזר article resolves, confirms 1944 Tel Aviv founding and 1951 move to Bnei Brak, but no Lilienblum address. חסידות ויז'ניץ article confirms dynasty/Bukovina origin, no Lilienblum. The Glatter PDF (in.bgu.ac.il) refused connection (ECONNREFUSED) — could NOT independently verify the quoted Lilienblum text; relying on the task-supplied index. No primary source anywhere confirms the number \"16\" for Eliezer Hager.",
        "corrections": "1) FOUNDER-vs-ADDRESS CONFLATION (main error): \"16\" belongs to רבי חיים מאיר הגר (Imrei Chaim), who lived at Lilienblum 16 until ~1951 — not to רבי אליעזר הגר (Damesek Eliezer), to whom Glatter ties Lilienblum WITHOUT a number. Either drop \"16\" or attribute it to Chaim Meir, not Eliezer. 2) ADDRESS confidence should be LOWERED — correctedAddress should flag that the house number is unverified for the named founder; keep address as \"לילינבלום, תל אביב\" without \"16\" unless tying it explicitly to Chaim Meir. 3) Keep the founder framing nuanced: Eliezer is correct for the Glatter Lilienblum/High-Holidays-hall claim; Chaim Meir is the one documented at #16. 4) DEATH YEAR 1946 is correct (the dynasty article's \"1945\" is the error, not the research). 5) Note Glatter's documented Vizhnitz rebbe-home with archival proof is Pierberg 35 — a separate, better-evidenced site; ensure these two are not merged. 6) \"medium\" confidence is roughly fair but the report should explicitly mark the house number as a conflation rather than a \"partially verified\" detail.",
        "dynastyCheck": "SOLID. Vizhnitz (ויז'ניץ), Kosov-Vizhnitz branch, Bukovina origin (Vyzhnytsia, today Ukraine), confirmed by both Glatter and Hebrew Wikipedia. Both rebbes (Eliezer Hager / Damesek Eliezer; Chaim Meir Hager / Imrei Chaim) are real and correctly named. Succession (Eliezer → brother Chaim Meir, who founded Kiryat Vizhnitz Bnei Brak) is accurate.",
        "founderCheck": "Eliezer Hager is REAL and correctly tied by Glatter to a Lilienblum residence + adjacent-hall High Holidays prayers. HOWEVER the founder is conflated with the house number: the \"16\" is documented for his successor brother Chaim Meir Hager, not for Eliezer. The research even concedes (in 'gaps') it could find no primary source placing #16 with Eliezer's residence/hall. Founder identity = correct; founder-to-house-number linkage = unsupported/conflated.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "1944 is DEFENSIBLE for Eliezer Hager's aliyah and Tel Aviv yeshiva founding (19 Apr 1944, confirmed by Wikipedia bio, yeshiva article, and Glatter). Caveat: the site's \"16\" attaches to Chaim Meir's residency (ending ~1951), so a single \"1944 founding\" label blurs two timelines (Eliezer 1944-1946; Chaim Meir's residency until 1951). Year itself = not fabricated.",
        "imageCheck": "SOLID. https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/he/e/ed/Damesekeliezer.JPG is a genuine PORTRAIT photograph (not a gravestone, not a fabricated URL) of Rabbi Eliezer Hager of Vizhnitz. License correctly stated as Public Domain in Israel (copyright expired, PD-Israel). Subject and caption match.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "House number '16' is conflated: it is documented for רבי חיים מאיר הגר (Imrei Chaim, resident until ~1951), NOT for רבי אליעזר הגר to whom the address/founder is attributed; Glatter gives Eliezer's Lilienblum entry NO house number.",
          "address 'לילינבלום 16' presented as the founder's (Eliezer's) site is unsupported — research itself admits no primary source places #16 with Eliezer's residence or the High Holidays hall.",
          "Risk of merging two distinct Glatter sites: Lilienblum (Eliezer, no number, no archival ref) vs the better-evidenced Pierberg 35 (תיק 650130, Agudat Damesek Eliezer) — they are different locations.",
          "Glatter PDF could not be independently retrieved (ECONNREFUSED), so the quoted Lilienblum passage rests solely on the task-supplied index, not verified at source.",
          "Minor: 'founded 1944' label collapses Eliezer's 1944-46 tenure and Chaim Meir's residency-to-1951 into one timeline."
        ]
