        "gaps": "קיימת אי-בהירות קלה בשנת המעבר לנחלת בנימין 23: רוב המקורות (חב\\\"דפדיה) נוקבים בתש\\\"ו (1946), אך גרסה אחת ציינה ת\\\"ש (1940). שנת ההתחלה המדויקת במונטיפיורי 36 (תרצ\\\"ה/1935) מבוססת על מקור חב\\\"די אחד. אין הפניה ארכיונית רשמית (את\\\"ב/אעת\\\"א) המאמתת ספציפית את הכתובת. גלאטר אינו מאשר את מונטיפיורי 36 בפירוט, אך גם אינו סותר את קיום הקהילה החב\\\"דית; השושלת (חב\\\"ד) מאומתת. הדיוקן הוא של האדמו\\\"ר הריי\\\"צ (לא ישב באתר זה), שכן זו קהילת חסידים מקומית ללא אדמו\\\"ר מקומי."
      },
      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "addressCheck": "PARTIALLY supported. Glatter does NOT support Montefiore 36. Glatter's only Chabad entry is a generic shtibel note (Chabad did not take root in TLV, moved its center to Kfar Chabad) with NO street, NO house number, and NO Tel Aviv Archive file reference -- unlike its rebbe-home entries that carry exact numbers (Dizengoff 36 Modzhitz, HaAvoda 15 Munkacs, Pierberg 35 Vizhnitz). So Glatter is SILENT here: it neither confirms nor contradicts. The Montefiore 36 address rests entirely on independent Chabad sources (Chabadpedia), which consistently state the community rented a small apartment-synagogue at Montefiore St 36. The claim's own glatterMatch_he honestly admits this, which is accurate. No Glatter-vs-research conflict to adjudicate on the address -- Glatter supplies no house-number data, so the Chabadpedia address stands as the best available evidence (community-wiki grade, not archival).",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed but adequate; all 4 cited URLs resolve and actually support what they are cited for -- no fabricated or dead links detected. (1) Chabadpedia 'Beit Knesset Merkaz Chabad TLV (Nachalat Binyamin)' supports Montefiore 36, Zevin, Krasik, the Gur shtibel on the floor above, and the move -- but it is a partisan community wiki, the weakest link for the load-bearing address. (2) HE-Wikipedia 'Eliezer Krasik' confirms 1936 appointment on Rayatz's recommendation and ~24-year tenure (1936-1960). (3) EN-Wikipedia 'Yosef Yitzchak Schneersohn' and (4) the Wikimedia Commons passport file both resolve and support the bio/image framing. Weakness: the single most consequential factual claim (the move year) is sourced to Chabadpedia, and the research MISREAD that very source (see corrections).",
        "dynastyCheck": "CORRECT and uncontested. Research and Glatter agree: Chabad-Lubavitch. Glatter lists Chabad as type 'shtibel' with the rebbe (Yosef Yitzchak Schneersohn) based abroad in Crown Heights -- fully consistent with the research framing this as a local community of chassidim, not a rebbe's residence. The dynastyBackground_he (founded by R. Shneur Zalman of Liadi, 18th c. Belarus; HBD = Chochma-Bina-Daat; Rayatz the 6th rebbe sat in Russia, Riga, Warsaw, then Crown Heights; center moved to Kfar Chabad founded 1949) is historically accurate. No mismatch.",
        "founderCheck": "DEFENSIBLE. The 'founder' is given as a group of Russian-immigrant Chabad chassidim (explicitly NOT a rebbe), which is the correct framing and matches Glatter's shtibel classification. The first community rabbi, R. Shlomo Yosef Zevin (later editor of the Talmudic Encyclopedia), is REAL and confirmed by multiple sources to have led the Montefiore community before moving to Jerusalem. His successor R. Chaim Eliezer Krasik (1898-1960) is REAL, confirmed appointed 1936 on the Rayatz's recommendation, serving ~24 years. Both figures are genuinely tied to THIS Montefiore community, not merely to the dynasty elsewhere. No fabricated person detected.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "PLAUSIBLE but thinly sourced for the START year; ERRONEOUS for the MOVE year. (a) Start of prayer at Montefiore 36 = tarsah/1935: rests on a single Chabad source and is not independently corroborated to the exact year; note Chabadpedia frames the immigration wave as tarsad-zayin (mid/late 1920s) and Zevin's aliyah is variously given as tarsad/1934. So 1935 is a reasonable approximation, not firmly fixed. (b) The move to Nachlat Binyamin 23: the main story_he says tasho/1946 and the gaps section calls 1946 the majority view -- this is INVERTED and WRONG. The primary cited source (Chabadpedia) explicitly states the move was in tash/1940, and the Zevin sources agree on 1940. See corrections.",
        "imageCheck": "REAL, free-licensed PORTRAIT -- passes. File:Yosef_Yitzchak_Schneersohn_Passport.jpg exists on Wikimedia Commons; the direct upload URL (upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/72/...) is valid. It is a genuine 1933 Latvian passport photographic portrait of the Rayatz -- not a gravestone, not AI-fabricated, not a broken URL. Licensing caveat: Commons tags it PD under Latvian copyright law (official state document), but the page also carries a 'possible wrong license' note, so the PD status is plausible but not airtight. Honest caption note: the research itself correctly states the Rayatz never sat at this site -- the portrait illustrates the rebbe on whose recommendation the local rabbi was appointed, which is a fair use of the image but is decorative rather than depicting the institution.",
        "corrections": "1) MOVE-YEAR (most significant): change the move to Nachlat Binyamin 23 from tasho/1946 to tash/1940. Chabadpedia (the primary cited source) explicitly says 'be-shnat tash avru ha-mitpallelim ... Nachalat Binyamin 23' = 1940, and the Zevin sources concur. The research not only picked the wrong year in story_he but inverted the evidence in gaps (it called 1946 the majority and 1940 the outlier; the reverse is true). 2) IMMIGRATION-WAVE wording: research says the group emigrated 'in the 1920s-1930s'; Chabadpedia dates the wave to tarsad-zayin (roughly mid/late 1920s) -- tighten this. 3) START-YEAR caveat: flag tarsah/1935 as resting on a single Chabad source and not independently fixed (Zevin's aliyah is given as ~1934). 4) CHEDER/Tomchei Tmimim 1936-1938: this specific detail was NOT found on the main Chabadpedia article in my checks; the Krasik bio supports a related 'Yeshivat Achei Tmimim' founded 1938. Treat the 1936-1938 'cheder at Montefiore 36' as plausible-but-under-sourced and label it accordingly. 5) IMAGE license: downgrade certainty -- note the 'possible wrong license' tag on Commons.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "MOVE YEAR: story_he says tasho/1946 -- WRONG; primary source (Chabadpedia) and Zevin sources say tash/1940. The gaps section additionally inverts the evidence (frames 1946 as majority view).",
          "START YEAR tarsah/1935: single-Chabad-source only; not independently corroborated to the exact year (Zevin aliyah variously 1934).",
          "CHEDER of Bnei/Tomchei Tmimim at Montefiore 1936-1938: not located on the main Chabadpedia article during verification; only a related 'Achei Tmimim' yeshiva (1938) is confirmed via the Krasik bio. Under-sourced.",
          "ADDRESS Montefiore 36: NOT in Glatter (no street/number/archive ref for Chabad); rests solely on Chabadpedia, a partisan community wiki.",
          "IMAGE license: Wikimedia Commons carries a 'possible wrong license' tag on the passport photo -- PD status plausible but not certain."
        ]
