        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "addressCheck": "Glatter does NOT support King George 15 as a historic Chabad institution — and the claim correctly says so. Verified: Glatter's single Chabad entry is a \"shtibel\" type tied to Rabbi Yosef Yitzchak Schneersohn (Crown Heights/NY, rebbe based abroad), with NO street, NO house number, and the explicit quote that \"Chabad did not take root in Tel Aviv... moved its center of activity to Kfar Chabad\" (1949). There is no King George / no #15 / no archival file number for any Chabad institution in Glatter. So Glatter cannot and does not support a pre-1980 Chabad shtibel/court at King George 15. The web independently confirms an ACTIVE modern Chabad house (\"ממעל ממש\" + \"מזוזה סנטר\") at המלך ג'ורג' 15 (official site mimaalmamash.com, Chabadpedia, Tel Aviv religious council rabanut.co.il, chabad.info, d.co.il/Golden Pages all list this exact address). Note: a separate Chabad Center sits at King George 30 (different number) — a potential conflation trap the claim avoids. Where Glatter and the open web agree: this address is a contemporary kiruv/Chabad-house, NOT a historic Hasidic court — so the map's \"synagogue/shtibel (historic)\" pin is an anachronism. The claim's mapErrorFlag \"not-a-synagogue\" (meaning: not a historic shtibel) and \"active\" status are both correct.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed but adequate, and honestly disclosed. Source 1 (Chabadpedia \"מרכז ממעל ממש\") resolves and directly supports founders (Tal Ziv, Yuval Barnes, Hanoch Weiner) and the Hanefesh Hashniya continuation. Source 3 (chabadtlv.org Geulat Yisrael) resolves and confirms the OLDER central-TA Chabad synagogue is a DIFFERENT address (Merkaz Baalei Melacha 16a, near Gan Sheinkin), founded 1933/dedicated 1937 — supporting the claim's contrast. Source 4 (Wikipedia Kfar Chabad) resolves and confirms 1949 founding on the initiative/blessing of Rabbi Yosef Yitzchak Schneersohn — corroborating Glatter. Source 2 (easy.co.il) returned 403, but the address is independently confirmed by the official site, Chabadpedia, rabanut.co.il, chabad.info and d.co.il, so the dead source is non-load-bearing. Glatter itself is verifiable: it is Michal Glatter, \"אדמו\"רים ברחובות תל אביב 1940–1965,\" BGU Iyunim issue 36 (in.bgu.ac.il/bgi/iyunim/36/36-Michal-Glatter.pdf) — a real peer-reviewed academic article. No image was claimed, correctly: there is no local rebbe portrait for a 21st-century kiruv center, so no risk of a fabricated/gravestone image.",
        "founderCheck": "Founders are REAL and specifically tied to THIS address — not merely the dynasty elsewhere. Tal Ziv (טל זיו) and Hanoch Weiner (חנוך וינר) are confirmed as the two founding Chabad rabbis of the King George 15 center by a Jan-2014 hagabay.net feature (\"the synagogue was established about eight years ago... by Rabbi Hanoch Weiner and Rabbi Tal Ziv; one had previously owned a watch shop at the location and they rented and converted it\"). Yuval Barnes (יובל ברנס) is added by Chabadpedia. The Hanefesh Hashniya (\"הנפש השנית\") connection is corroborated. These are contemporary kiruv activists, NOT historic rebbes — consistent with the claim. Caveat: these are founders of the MODERN center, not of any historic court; the claim states this correctly and assigns no rebbe-of-a-court to this address.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "The claim's \"unknown (post-2000)\" is defensible but under-precise. Independent evidence narrows it: the Jan-6-2014 hagabay.net article says the synagogue was founded \"about eight years ago\" (≈2006), and a 2021 Chabad article says it has operated \"close to 20 years\" (≈2002–2006). So the best estimate is circa 2006, not merely \"post-2000.\" Recommend updating foundingYear to \"c. 2006 (modern Chabad house).\" This does not change the verdict — it remains firmly a contemporary, post-1980 institution, so the map's historic-shtibel framing is still anachronistic.",
        "dynastyCheck": "Dynasty attribution (Chabad) holds. The center is a genuine Chabad-Lubavitch house (official site \"בית חב\"ד קינג ג'ורג'\", Chabadpedia, chabad.info, rabanut.co.il). The dynastyBackground (Schneur Zalman of Liadi; חב\"ד = Chochma-Bina-Daat; Yosef Yitzchak's flight to USA; Menachem Mendel Schneersohn leading from Crown Heights from 1951; shlichus/kiruv emphasis) is accurate. Glatter's framing that Chabad's TA presence is modern outreach rather than a transplanted local court is fully supported.",
        "imageCheck": "No image claimed — correct and appropriate. The entry attaches no portrait, with the honest rationale that no local rebbe is tied to this address. There is therefore no fabricated URL, no gravestone-as-portrait, and no free-license-portrait error to flag. This is the right call for a 21st-century kiruv center.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "ANACHRONISM (the core issue, correctly self-flagged): mapping King George 15 as a historic 'synagogue/shtibel' is wrong — it is a c.2006 Chabad house, not a pre-1980 Hasidic court. The map pin is the error, not the research.",
          "IMPRECISION: foundingYear 'unknown (post-2000)' should be 'c. 2006' per hagabay.net (2014, 'about eight years ago') and a 2021 Chabad article ('close to 20 years').",
          "POTENTIAL CONFLATION TRAP (avoided): a different Chabad Center exists at King George 30, and the historic Chabad synagogue 'Geulat Yisrael' is at Merkaz Baalei Melacha 16a — the claim correctly keeps these distinct.",
