          "Glatter's Chabad 'shtibel' type label refers to a rebbe-based-abroad entry with no TA address; it must NOT be read as evidence of a King George 15 shtibel — claim reads it correctly."
        ],
        "corrections": "1) Founding year: change \"unknown (post-2000)\" to \"c. 2006\" — supported by hagabay.net (Jan 2014: founded \"about eight years ago\") and a 2021 Chabad article (\"close to 20 years\"). 2) Replace the 403 easy.co.il source with the official site https://mimaalmamash.com/ and/or the Tel Aviv religious-council listing https://rabanut.co.il/synagogue/ממעל-ממש/ (both confirm address המלך ג'ורג' 15 and Chabad-house status). 3) Keep mapErrorFlag \"not-a-synagogue\" and the anachronism conclusion — they are correct: the pin should not represent a historic Hasidic court. 4) Optionally note the nearby distractor (Chabad Center at King George 30) to pre-empt future conflation. 5) Glatter and the research do NOT actually disagree here — both agree there was no historic Chabad court in TA proper (moved to Kfar Chabad, 1949); the research correctly uses Glatter as negative evidence rather than overriding it. Bottom line: the entry's facts and reasoning are sound; only the founding-year precision and one dead URL need fixing, and the underlying map data point is an anachronistic mislabel that the research correctly identifies."
