        "addressCheck": "NOT SUPPORTED. No source ties Rabbi Epstein, his home, or \"Esh Dat\" to Yehuda HaLevi 8. Every source that gives any location says the opposite direction: Hebrew Wikipedia states he lived on Rothschild Boulevard until his death (\"בתל אביב התגורר בשדרות רוטשילד עד סוף ימיו\"), and that he founded a synagogue on Rothschild Blvd at the corner of Luntz St, near Bilu school. A tlv100 (tlv100.net) page even lists \"בית מורי (דירת הרב אפשטיין)\" mapped to the Rothschild 126-128 block. MyTzadik and zadikim.com only say \"south Tel Aviv.\" Yehuda HaLevi 8 is the research author's own admitted speculation (\"אפשרי אך לא אומת באף מקור\"). Verdict: the address is fabricated/unverified; best-supported location is Rothschild Blvd (synagogue at Rothschild x Luntz; residence cited as Rothschild, ~126-128). The Glatter record for Ozarov gives NO street/number, so it neither confirms nor corrects Yehuda HaLevi 8.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed but the cited URLs are real and resolve. Hebrew + English Wikipedia, MyTzadik, zadikim.com, OU.org, Hamichlol all exist and broadly support the PERSON (Moshe Yechiel Halevi Epstein, Ozarov-Chentshin Rebbe, b. 1889 d. 27 Jan 1971, Israel Prize 1968, author of Esh Dat 11 vols and Be'er Moshe, aliyah 17 Tammuz 5713/1953, lived near Chazon Ish in Bnei Brak then moved to Tel Aviv, buried Bnei Brak/Shomrei Shabbat cemetery). However NONE of these sources support the specific address, and the research honestly flags this. The sources do NOT support \"Esh Dat\" as an institution/beit midrash — every source treats Esh Dat strictly as the title of his book. No free-licensed portrait was located (research correctly omitted an image).",
        "corrections": "1) ADDRESS: Replace \"יהודה הלוי 8\" with Rothschild Boulevard. Best-documented: synagogue at Rothschild Blvd corner of Luntz St (near Bilu school); residence cited on Rothschild Blvd (tlv100 places his apartment at the Rothschild 126-128 block). Yehuda HaLevi 8 has zero support and should be dropped, not merely flagged \"low confidence.\" 2) \"אש דת\" IS A BOOK, NOT A MOSAD/BEIT MIDRASH. The claim of a \"מוסד אש דת / אגודת אוז'רוב-חנצ'ין... מכון להוצאת ספריו\" at Yehuda HaLevi 8 is unsupported conflation; Esh Dat is his 11-volume work (c. 1950-1963). Remove the invented \"beit midrash Esh Dat.\" 3) MAP/COORDINATE ERROR: the research itself notes lat 32.06121 falls in north TA (Kikar HaMedina), inconsistent with both Yehuda HaLevi and Rothschild — internal contradiction; coordinate is wrong. 4) DYNASTY FOUNDER nuance: founder is Rabbi Aryeh Leib of Ozarov (rav in Ozarov 1812, rebbe 1815, disciple of the Chozeh of Lublin), not \"founded... died ~1827\" as the only framing — 1827 is a death-date guess; he later moved to Ovruch. The \"Ozarov-Chentshin\" combined name is real but arises because Epstein was maternal grandson of R' Chaim Shmuel of Chentshin (he held both courts) — confirmed by Hebrew Wikipedia. 5) GLATTER vs RESEARCH name order: Glatter lists \"רבי יחיאל משה אפשטיין\"; correct/standard order is \"משה יחיאל\" (per Wikipedia and his works). Minor Glatter inversion; same person. 6) FOUNDING YEAR 1953 is defensible as his aliyah year (17 Tammuz 5713 = 1953) and matches Glatter's year \"1953\" and origin \"New York\" (he came from the US) — this is the one solid pillar. But \"founding\" of an institution at this address in 1953 is not established; he moved to TA only after Chazon Ish died (late 1953), and no institution-founding at any specific TA address is documented.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "FABRICATED/UNVERIFIED ADDRESS: 'יהודה הלוי 8' — no source; contradicted by Rothschild Blvd sourcing.",
          "CONFLATION: 'מוסד אש דת / בית מדרש אש דת' presented as an institution at the address — Esh Dat is his BOOK (11 vols), not a mosad. No source describes an 'Esh Dat' beit midrash.",
          "INTERNAL CONTRADICTION: map coordinate lat 32.06121 is in north TA (Kikar HaMedina), inconsistent with Yehuda HaLevi 8 AND with the true Rothschild location.",
          "OVER-PRECISE FOUNDER FRAMING: Ozarov 'founded... נפטר תקפ\"ז/1827' — 1827 is an uncertain death date; founder R' Aryeh Leib became rebbe ~1815 and later relocated to Ovruch.",
