        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "addressCheck": "SUPPORTED (number 36), but with a caveat about Glatter. The corrected house number \"דיזנגוף 36\" is independently corroborated by the open web: yeshiva.org.il and Hamichlol explicitly state Rabbi Shmuel Eliyahu Taub established his Modzitz beit midrash at Dizengoff 36 (after starting on Lilienblum). So the 87→36 correction (mapErrorFlag \"wrong-number\") is defensible on open-web grounds ALONE, independent of Glatter. HOWEVER: I could NOT open the Glatter PDF (https://in.bgu.ac.il/bgi/iyunim/36/36-Michal-Glatter.pdf) — it returned ECONNREFUSED via WebFetch and timed out (HTTP 000) via curl on multiple attempts. Therefore I cannot independently confirm that Glatter actually contains the quote \"מרכז חסידות מודז'יץ ... דיזנגוף 36\", the origin \"קראטשוב (Kratshov)\", the year 1936, or the archival file numbers (תיק 1870360, מסמכים 190260/190293/190295/190569/190567). Those Glatter-specific details are UNVERIFIED. The number 36 itself, though, stands on the open web.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed. The Wikipedia/Yeshiva/Hamichlol/NLI/mytzadik sources are real, resolve, and genuinely support the core biography (founder identity, dynasty, dates of the Rebbes, Lilienblum→Dizengoff progression, move to Bnei Brak). The Wikimedia image file is real, exists, and is a genuine public-domain PORTRAIT photograph of the Rebbe (source modzitz.org, PD-Poland). The ONE critical source I could not verify is the most load-bearing one for the geographic correction: the Glatter academic PDF at in.bgu.ac.il is unreachable from this environment (connection refused / timeout), so every Glatter-exclusive detail (Kratshov origin, year 1936, the exact archival file/document numbers, the \"built as a large beit midrash with prayer room and library, registered to amutat Beit Modzitz\" framing) rests entirely on the supplied JSON and could not be confirmed against the primary document.",
        "corrections": "1) FOUNDING YEAR — strongest error. The claim's headline year \"1936 (לפי גלאטר)\" is almost certainly wrong/anachronistic for THIS beit midrash. Open web (yeshiva.org.il, Hamichlol) dates the Dizengoff 36 beit midrash to תשט\"ז / 1956. Moreover the founder Shmuel Eliyahu only made aliyah in 1935 and only became Admor (3rd) in 1947 on his father's death — so a 1936 \"center in his leadership\" at Dizengoff is impossible. Glatter's 1936, if real, likely refers to a much earlier/registration date or is simply an error; it should NOT be presented as the founding year of this institution. Use 1956 (תשט\"ז) for the beit midrash, and flag Glatter's 1936 as disputed/likely erroneous. The JSON's foundingYear/gaps already hedge this, but the top-line confidence \"high\" overstates it. 2) MOVE TO BNEI BRAK — open web gives a specific date: ל\"ג בעומר תשנ\"ה / 1995, when Rabbi Yisrael Dan Taub (4th Admor, successor — NOT Shmuel Eliyahu) inaugurated the Habakkuk St. beit midrash in Bnei Brak while keeping the old Dizengoff hall operating. The yeshiva \"Amrei Shaul\" named for his father was founded by Shmuel Eliyahu in 1981 (a separate event). The claim conflates these and says \"המקורות חלוקים בין אמצע שנות ה-70 לבין 1981/1995\" — the 1995 figure is the well-attested one; \"mid-1970s\" appears unsupported. 3) GENEALOGY/SUCCESSION — minor: Shmuel Eliyahu was the SON of the 2nd Admor Shaul Yedidya and the GRANDSON of founder Yisrael; he was the 3rd Admor. The JSON gets the Admor numbers right but its prose is easy to misread. The dynasty's CURRENT Rebbe / Bnei Brak center is under the 4th-5th generation (Yisrael Dan Taub d.2006, then Chaim Shaul Taub) — the \"~400 families\" figure is unverified. 4) ORIGIN \"קראטשוב/Kratshov\" (from Glatter) conflicts with the well-established town of origin Dęblin/Modzitz; this Glatter-only origin tag is unverified and suspicious — do NOT treat it as the dynasty's town of origin. 5) Lower the geographic-correction confidence from \"high\" to \"medium\" until the Glatter PDF can be opened, since the 1936 date attached to that same Glatter entry is demonstrably problematic.",
        "dynastyCheck": "HOLDS. Modzitz is a real Polish Hasidic dynasty (\"ממלכת הנגינה\"), founded by Rabbi Yisrael Taub (Divrei Yisrael) in Dęblin/Modzitz ~1889. The Rebbe in question, Shmuel Eliyahu Taub, is genuinely the 3rd Admor of Modzitz and genuinely associated with Tel Aviv. Dynasty attribution is correct. The only caveat is the Glatter-only origin tag \"Kratshov\" which conflicts with the established Modzitz/Dęblin origin and is unverified.",
        "founderCheck": "REAL and TIED TO THIS ADDRESS. Rabbi Shmuel Eliyahu Taub (1905–1984), 3rd Admor of Modzitz, is independently documented (Wikipedia, NLI, yeshiva.org.il, Hamichlol, mytzadik). He is specifically tied to a Modzitz beit midrash on Dizengoff Street (after Lilienblum), and yeshiva.org.il/Hamichlol specifically place it at Dizengoff 36. So this is NOT a case of merely the dynasty-elsewhere; the founder→this-address link is supported. Caveat: he became Admor only in 1947 and the hall dates to ~1956, so he cannot be the founder of anything at this address in 1936.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "NOT defensible as stated. \"1936 (לפי גלאטר)\" is anachronistic and contradicted by open web, which dates the Dizengoff 36 beit midrash to 1956 (תשט\"ז). The founder only made aliyah 1935 and became Admor 1947. Correct year for the institution: ~1956. Glatter's 1936 should be flagged as disputed/likely erroneous, not used as the headline founding year.",
        "imageCheck": "PASS. https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shmuel_Eliyahu_Taub_MODZITZER.jpg is a real file that exists on Wikimedia Commons (uploaded 2007, 365×530px). It is a genuine PORTRAIT photograph of Rabbi Shmuel Eliyahu Taub — not a gravestone, not a fabricated URL. License is Public Domain (PD-Poland: published without copyright notice before 1994-05-23, also PD in the US). Source modzitz.org. Caption correctly identifies him. No issues.",
