      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "shaky",
        "addressCheck": "NO — neither Glatter nor any independent source supports \"HaPalmach 10\". Glatter's Nadvorna entry (רבי איתמר רוזנבוים ובנו חיים מרדכי / ירושלים / 1950 / rebbe-home) has NO street, NO house number, and NO archival reference — unlike the entries it CAN pin down (Modzhitz=Dizengoff 36 + תיק 1870360; Vizhnitz=Piarberg 35 + תיק 650130; Bohush=Rothschild 112 + תיק 81120; Munkacs=HaAvoda 15; Stratyn=Hillel HaZaken 10). So Glatter explicitly does NOT override anything toward HaPalmach 10; it is silent on the address. The Tel Aviv Religious Council database lists HaPalmach 10 as synagogue \"בית יינון\" of nusach עדות המזרח (Mizrahi/Sephardi), phone 03-6314311 — NOT an Ashkenazi-Hasidic Nadvorna shtibel. Independent sources (he.wikipedia, en.wikipedia, hamichlol) place the beit midrash only in \"Yad Eliyahu neighborhood\" with NO street/number. Confirmed: HaPalmach street IS within Yad Eliyahu (rova 9), so the neighborhood-level placement is plausible, but the specific house \"HaPalmach 10\" is positively contradicted (different congregation there). Map house number is unverifiable-to-wrong. The research's own low confidence and \"unverifiable\" flag are appropriate.",
        "sourceQuality": "Mixed but mostly genuine. The 5 cited open-web URLs all resolve and substantively support the institution-level claims: he.wikipedia איתמר_רוזנבוים (immigration ~תשכ\"ט/1968-69, Yad Eliyahu, died כ\"ב סיון תשל\"ג/22 Jun 1973, buried Mount of Olives, father רבי מאיר מקרעטשניף, son רבי חיים מרדכי), he.wikipedia חסידות_נדבורנה, he.wikipedia יצחק_אייזיק_רוזנבוים (succeeded father at Yad Eliyahu beit midrash, moved to Bnei Brak תשמ\"א/1981, first Zutchka admor), hamichlol רבי איתמר רוזנבוים, and the Religious Council directory (Beit Yinon at HaPalmach 10). en.wikipedia \"Isamar Rosenbaum\" also resolves but gives immigration as 1970 from Washington Heights NYC — a third date variant. NONE of the cited sources mentions HaPalmach 10 — the address claim has zero positive sourcing. Glatter is internally authoritative for institutions with archival file numbers, but this particular Nadvorna entry carries no file number, so it cannot back the address.",
        "corrections": "1) FOUNDER OF DYNASTY (factual error in dynastyBackground_he): The claim states \"מייסדה נחשב רבי מרדכי מנדבורנה\". This is wrong/conflated. The eponymous founder of Nadvorna Hasidism is רבי ישכר בער (Issachar Ber) לייפר, the first to serve as admor in the town of Nadvorna (deeper root: רבי מאיר הגדול מפרמישלאן). רבי מרדכי מנדבורנה (1824-1894) was the SECOND admor of the central court, not the founder. Correct to: \"מייסדה רבי ישכר בער לייפר מנדבורנה (משורש רבי מאיר מפרמישלאן)\". 2) INSTITUTION FOUNDER: Rabbi Itamar Rosenbaum is real and correctly tied to a Yad Eliyahu beit midrash, succeeded by son Yitzhak Aizik (first Zutchka admor, moved to Bnei Brak 1981) — all verified. 3) YEAR: Glatter's 1950 is NOT the founding year of this beit midrash and the research correctly rejects it for that purpose. Best-supported immigration/founding window is 1968-1970 (he.wiki ~1968/תשכ\"ט; en.wiki 1970). The research's \"1967-1969\" is slightly early on the low end; tighten to ~1968-1970. Where Glatter (1950) and the research disagree on the beit-midrash founding date, the RESEARCH is correct — 1950 at most reflects the family's earlier arrival in Israel (via Jerusalem) or son Chaim Mordechai's settlement, not Itamar's Yad Eliyahu court. 4) ADDRESS: Replace \"HaPalmach 10\" with \"Yad Eliyahu neighborhood, exact street/number undocumented.\" HaPalmach 10 currently houses the Mizrahi synagogue Beit Yinon, not a Nadvorna shtibel — the map's specific house number is unsupported and likely erroneous. 5) IMAGE: Correctly omitted — no free-licensed portrait exists (only a copyrighted Dynasty Auctions oil painting, gravestone photos, and a different family's photo). Do not attach an image. NOTE one minor research wording issue: it calls Yitzhak Aizik the one who \"ייסד את חסידות זוטשקא\" (founded Zutchka) — sources frame him as the FIRST admor of Zutchka rather than founder of a new movement; acceptable but soften.",
        "dynastyCheck": "Dynasty attribution (Nadvorna / נדבורנה, Galician-Bukovinian) is CORRECT for the institution and for Rabbi Itamar Rosenbaum (son of Rabbi Meir of Kretchnif, a Nadvorna offshoot; \"האדמו\"ר הזקן מנדבורנה\"). Branches Kretchnif and Zutchka correctly identified. HOWEVER the dynasty BACKGROUND contains a founder error: it names רבי מרדכי מנדבורנה as founder, whereas the actual eponymous founder is רבי ישכר בער לייפר (root: רבי מאיר מפרמישלאן). World center today in Bnei Brak — correct.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "Defensible only as a window, not as stated against Glatter. Glatter=1950 is NOT the beit-midrash founding date and the research rightly rejects it. Independent sources: he.wikipedia/hamichlol ~תשכ\"ט (1968-69); en.wikipedia 1970 (from Washington Heights). Research's \"1967-1969\" is slightly too early on the low end; best supported is ~1968-1970. Verdict: research is correct over Glatter on the founding-year question; minor tightening recommended.",
        "founderCheck": "Institution founder Rabbi Itamar Rosenbaum (1886-1973), \"האדמו\"ר הזקן מנדבורנה,\" is REAL and verified across he/en Wikipedia and Hamichlol: immigrated ~1968-1970, established a beit midrash in Yad Eliyahu, Tel Aviv, died 22 June 1973 (כ\"ב סיון תשל\"ג), buried on Mount of Olives. Succeeded by son Rabbi Yitzhak Aizik Rosenbaum (first Zutchka admor), who moved the center to Bnei Brak in 1981. BUT he is tied only to \"Yad Eliyahu,\" NOT specifically to HaPalmach 10 — no source links him to that house number. Founder is real; address linkage is not established.",
        "imageCheck": "No image attached, which is CORRECT. Searches surface only a copyrighted oil-on-canvas portrait at Dynasty Auctions, gravestone/memorial photos, and unrelated family photos. No free-licensed (Wikimedia Commons / public-domain) photographic PORTRAIT of Rabbi Itamar Rosenbaum was found. Wikidata Q12260267 exists but without a free portrait image. Research's decision to omit an image is accurate and well-justified.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "FOUNDER CONFLATION: dynastyBackground_he names רבי מרדכי מנדבורנה as dynasty founder; actual founder is רבי ישכר בער לייפר (root רבי מאיר מפרמישלאן). Mordechai was the 2nd central admor.",
          "ADDRESS UNSUPPORTED: 'HaPalmach 10' has no positive source; Glatter gives no street/number for Nadvorna and no archival file; Religious Council lists HaPalmach 10 as Mizrahi synagogue 'Beit Yinon', not Nadvorna.",
          "GLATTER YEAR ANACHRONISM (already flagged by research, correctly): Glatter's 1950 does not match the 1968-1970 founding of Itamar's Yad Eliyahu beit midrash.",
