        "gaps": "השיוך במפה (\"נחמני 37 - נדבורנה\") אינו נתמך לא בגלאטר ולא במקורות הפתוחים. שתי בעיות: (1) הדינסטיה — נחמני מזוהה עם סדיגורה (רבי אברהם יעקב פרידמן, בית נושא-חן), ולא עם נדבורנה; נדבורנה פעלה בתל אביב בשכונת יד אליהו (רבי איתמר רוזנבוים, מ-1969), ומרכזה בבני ברק. גלאטר רושם נדבורנה כ\"בית אדמו\\\"ר\" ללא רחוב/מספר. (2) מספר הבית — הכתובת ההיסטורית של סדיגורה היא נחמני 27 (פינת אחד העם 45), לא 37; נחמני 37 מופיע רק כפרויקט נדל\"ן עכשווי ללא בית כנסת מתועד. לא ברור אם הכניסה במפה היא טעות מספר בית בלבד (שצריכה לקרוא 27/סדיגורה) או בלבול דינסטיות מוחלט. לא נמצא ביסוס לקיום בית כנסת נדבורנאי ברחוב נחמני בכל מספר. לא נכללה תמונה: הכתובת משויכת בטעות, ולא נפתח דף רישיון חופשי מאומת לדיוקן אדמו\"ר רלוונטי. הסטטוס הנוכחי של המבנה אינו ודאי."
      },
      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "addressCheck": "Glatter does NOT place Nadvorna on Nachmani at all. In the authoritative Glatter index, Nadvorna (רבי איתמר רוזנבוים ובנו חיים מרדכי, origin Jerusalem, year 1950, type rebbe-home) is listed with NO street and NO house number and NO archival file — confirming Glatter never locates Nadvorna on Nachmani 37 or any Nachmani address. Glatter places Sadigura (רבי אברהם יעקב פרידמן, Vienna, 1939, rebbe-home) on רחוב פנקס, and explicitly states Sadigura moved its center to Pinkas in the 1960s. So Glatter does not directly support EITHER \"Nachmani 37\" or \"Nachmani 27\" as a house number — it has no Nachmani entry whatsoever and assigns Sadigura's Glatter-era address to Pinkas. The Nachmani-27 corrected address is supported by OPEN WEB (Hebrew Wikipedia \"Sadigura\" article says the rebbe opened a synagogue \"on Nachmani Street\"; the golden-lotus.co.il \"Beit Nosse Chen\" page gives the exact corner Achad Ha'am 45 / Nachmani 27 and names Rabbi Avraham Yaakov Friedman 1884-1960 as its most famous resident from 1937 for 22 years until his 1960 death). Net: the research's core thesis — that \"Nachmani 37 - Nadvorna\" is a wrong-dynasty/wrong-number map error, and the historically documented Nachmani address is Sadigura at no. 27 — is well supported by both Glatter (negatively, by absence) and the open web (positively). The mapErrorFlag \"wrong-dynasty\" is justified. House number 37 is unsupported by any source for any synagogue; only no. 27 (Sadigura) is documented.",
        "sourceQuality": "Strong and internally consistent. All five cited URLs resolve and each actually supports the specific claim attached to it: (1) he.wikipedia \"Itamar Rosenbaum\" confirms aliyah 1969, settled in Yad Eliyahu, born 1886 / died 1973, NO mention of Nachmani — supports Nadvorna being in Yad Eliyahu, not Nachmani. (2) he.wikipedia \"Nadvorna Hasidic Center\" confirms today's center is in Kiryat Nadvorna, Bnei Brak (Admor MiNadvorna St. 72), no Tel Aviv/Nachmani link. (3) he.wikipedia \"Sadigura\" confirms the rebbe opened a synagogue on Nachmani Street, later disputes moved the beit midrash, and the nephew reopened on Pinkas in the 1960s — matches Glatter's Pinkas note. (4) golden-lotus.co.il \"Beit Nosse Chen\" confirms Achad Ha'am 45 / Nachmani 27, architect Yosef Berlin 1925, and Rabbi Avraham Yaakov Friedman (1884-1960) as resident from 1937 for 22 years. (5) project-tlv.info confirms \"Nachmani 37\" exists only as a real-estate project listing with no synagogue/Hasidic institution documented. A targeted Hebrew search for a Nadvorna synagogue on Nachmani returned nothing, reinforcing the absence.",
        "dynastyCheck": "The map's \"Nadvorna\" attribution to Nachmani is unsupported and almost certainly a conflation/error. Nadvorna's documented Tel Aviv presence is Yad Eliyahu (Rabbi Itamar Rosenbaum from 1969), with the dynasty's center now in Bnei Brak. Glatter lists Nadvorna with no street. Nachmani is documented for Sadigura. The research's wrong-dynasty diagnosis holds. One nuance the research correctly flags: it is unclear whether the map entry is a pure dynasty confusion or a house-number typo plus dynasty swap — both errors are present (wrong dynasty AND a house number, 37, that no source ties to any synagogue).",
        "founderCheck": "Correctly handled. The research states no founder is relevant to Nadvorna at this address and identifies the genuine historical figure on Nachmani as Rabbi Avraham Yaakov Friedman of Sadigura (1884-1960) — corroborated by the Beit Nosse Chen page and the Sadigura Wikipedia article. Note a minor internal inconsistency in the research's dynastyBackground for Nadvorna: it gives Itamar Rosenbaum's dates as 1886-1973 (תרמ\"ו–תשל\"ג), which matches Wikipedia (born 1886, died 1973); that is accurate. The Sadigura rebbe's birth year appears as 1886 in the research's story (implied via \"כעשרים ושתיים שנים\") but Beit Nosse Chen and Wikipedia give 1884-1960 — the research's correctedAddress block correctly uses Friedman without a wrong birth year, so no fabrication, but anyone citing \"1884\" should use the Nosse-Chen/Wikipedia figure, not 1886.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "Defensible. For Nadvorna the research says foundingYear is unknown at this (wrong) address, which is correct. For the Sadigura reality on Nachmani it gives 1937 (arrival of Rabbi Avraham Yaakov Friedman), corroborated by Beit Nosse Chen (\"relocated to Tel Aviv in 1937 and resided 22 years until 1960\"). Glatter dates Sadigura's rebbe-home entry to 1939 (year of arrival in Israel per Glatter), and the move to Pinkas to the 1960s. The 1937 (open web) vs 1939 (Glatter) discrepancy is a known type of variance — 1937 is the Beit Nosse Chen / Wikipedia arrival-in-Tel-Aviv year; 1939 is Glatter's general \"arrived in Israel\" tag for the Vienna emigres. Neither is fabricated; flag only that the two sources differ by ~2 years.",
        "imageCheck": "No image was included, which the research explicitly and correctly justifies (the address is misattributed, so no relevant rebbe portrait is asserted). No fabricated image URL, no gravestone, no risk here. Acceptable.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "House number 37: NO source ties any synagogue or Hasidic institution to Nachmani 37 — it appears only as a contemporary real-estate project (project-tlv.info). The map's '37' is unsupported.",
          "Glatter does NOT corroborate 'Nachmani 27' as a house number. Glatter has no Nachmani entry at all and assigns Sadigura to Pinkas. The Nachmani-27 address rests solely on open-web sources (Beit Nosse Chen / Wikipedia), not on Glatter — the research slightly overstates Glatter's support when it implies Glatter backs the Nachmani-27 history; Glatter only backs the Pinkas move.",
          "Year discrepancy: research/open-web give Sadigura arrival 1937; Glatter dates the Sadigura rebbe-home to 1939. Minor, non-fabricated.",
          "Sadigura rebbe birth year: Beit Nosse Chen and Wikipedia give 1884-1960; ensure any citation uses 1884, not a different year.",
          "The research's claim that 'נחמני מזוהה היסטורית עם סדיגורה' is supported, but the Wikipedia Sadigura article says only 'a synagogue on Nachmani Street' without a number — the precise number 27 comes only from the Beit Nosse Chen page (Achad Ha'am 45 / Nachmani 27 corner). Single-source for the exact number."
        ],
        "corrections": "1) The map entry 'נחמני 37 - נדבורנה' is a double error: wrong dynasty (Nadvorna was never on Nachmani; it was in Yad Eliyahu from 1969 under R. Itamar Rosenbaum, center now in Bnei Brak) AND a house number (37) that no source ties to any synagogue. 2) The historically documented Hasidic site on Nachmani is SADIGURA at no. 27 (corner Achad Ha'am 45, 'Beit Nosse Chen'), home of Rabbi Avraham Yaakov Friedman (1884-1960) from 1937 until his death in 1960; Sadigura later moved its center to Pinkas in the 1960s. 3) State precisely that Glatter does NOT support either Nachmani 37 or 27 — Glatter lists Nadvorna with no street and lists Sadigura on Pinkas; the Nachmani-27 history is established by open-web sources, not Glatter. Where Glatter and open web 'disagree', they do not actually conflict: Glatter simply records Sadigura's later Pinkas address, while the open web records its earlier Nachmani-27 address — both are correct for different periods. 4) Use Sadigura rebbe dates 1884-1960. 5) Treat the exact 'no. 27' as single-sourced (Beit Nosse Chen) since Wikipedia says only 'Nachmani Street'. Overall the research's adversarial correction of the map is sound; its only overreach is implying Glatter affirmatively supports the Nachmani-27 location, when Glatter is merely silent on Nachmani and the support is open-web."
