        "sourceQuality": "Mixed but mostly adequate. The two Wikipedia sources resolve and genuinely support the dynasty/leadership narrative. The rabanut.co.il source resolves and confirms the name and Oliphant 17 address (though it lists a gabai \"Hanan Stoyser,\" not Rabbi Auerbach, and does not itself state \"Sadigura\"). The 4th cited \"source\" is a Waze live-map link for the SEPARATE Pinkas synagogue — a navigation URL, not a citable authority. Missing from the research's own source list (but found in verification): project-tlv.info and michaelarch.wordpress.com, which reveal the Antopol-survivor origin of the building and contradict the \"school building\" framing — a material omission.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "WRONG HEBREW DATE: story_he writes the death as 'ה' בטבת תרפ\"א, 24 בדצמבר 1960'. תרפ\"א = 5681 = 1920/21, which contradicts the 1960 Gregorian date. Correct Hebrew year is תשכ\"א (5721). All authoritative sources give ה' בטבת תשכ\"א = 24 December 1960. This is an internal contradiction / transcription error.",
          "BUILDING-TYPE ERROR: 'עבר למבנה בית הספר ברחוב אוליפנט' (moved to the school building on Oliphant). Independent sources show Oliphant 17 is a PURPOSE-BUILT 1960 synagogue (cornerstone 1955) founded by Antopol survivors, not a former school. The 'school building' detail (taken from Wikipedia) is uncorroborated and likely wrong.",
          "GLATTER CONFLICT (unflagged in glatterMatch_he, which is left empty): Glatter indexes Sadigura under the SAME named rebbe 'רבי אברהם יעקב פרידמן' (Vienna, 1939) but locates the center on פנקס, not Oliphant. The research assigns Glatter's Pinkas entry to the OTHER branch (Mordechai Shalom Yosef / Knesset Mordechai). But Glatter's named person is Avraham Yaakov, not Mordechai Shalom Yosef — so the research's split is not fully consistent with Glatter's own text. Glatter does NOT support Oliphant 17; it supports Pinkas.",
