        "addressCheck": "CORRECT and well-handled. The claim itself is a debunking: it asserts that Allenby 58 is NOT and never was a Hasidic synagogue, and that the real Karlin-Stolin center in Tel Aviv is at Bar Kochva 52. The Glatter index supports this entirely: Karlin-Stolin (קרלין־סטולין) appears in Glatter ONLY in the general list of \"other Hasidic centers in the city\" as a shtibel type, with NO street, NO house number, NO year, and NO archival reference (quote: \"מרכזים חסידיים אחרים בעיר היו עבור החסידויות האלה: ... קרלין־סטולין\"). Glatter contains no entry tying any institution to Allenby 58. So Glatter neither contradicts nor supports an Allenby 58 synagogue — consistent with the research's conclusion that the map pin is an error. The corrected address (Bar Kochva 52) is independently confirmed by web sources (TJT/zmanei tfila listing TE56691, kipa.co.il \"Bar Kochva\" synagogue entry, GuideStar registered amuta). Note: Glatter does NOT itself give Bar Kochva 52 — that house number comes from the open web, not the academic source. The research is transparent about this gap (it says Glatter does not document a precise address). No house-number fabrication detected.",
