      "verdict": {
        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "addressCheck": "PARTIAL - supported on street, NOT on house number. Glatter supports Rashi street (rechov Rashi) as the site of a Vizhnitz shtibel, but gives NO house number. WebSearch extraction of the Glatter PDF confirms: \"In 1943, members of the Vizhnitz synagogue (Shtibl) on Rashi Street in Tel Aviv requested permission from the Tel Aviv municipality to use a school auditorium for High Holiday prayers\" (archival ref chativa 8, michal 1084, tik 2288). The map's \"Rashi 1\" is therefore unverified. The research JSON correctly flags this in its gaps and correctedAddress fields. The \"1\" should be treated as an unconfirmed map artifact. Note: the bgu.ac.il PDF host returned ECONNREFUSED to the fetcher (likely geofenced to Israel), but the search engine had already indexed and extracted the matching passage.",
        "sourceQuality": "Good. All four cited URLs are real and authoritative. (1) Glatter, Iyunim BeTekumat Israel 36 (Ben-Gurion University) - confirmed to exist and to contain the Rashi-street/Vizhnitz/1943 claim via search indexing plus a mirror on kotar.cet.ac.il; the PDF blocks foreign fetches but is genuine. (2) He-Wikipedia Weinberg (Slonim) - resolves; confirms Tiomkin street, 1935 aliyah, 1978 death, small beit midrash. (3) He-Wikipedia Vizhnitz - real. (4) En-Wikipedia Vizhnitz dynasty (Chaim Hager of Ottynia, d.1931) - real. Independent corroboration from hamichlol.org.il Otynia article: an Otynia synagogue did exist in Tel Aviv, and founder Chaim Hager died 1931.",
        "founderCheck": "Real and correctly scoped - see founder field.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "DEFENSIBLE. The JSON does not assert a precise founding year; it states the shtibel \"operated by 1943 at the latest\" based on the summer-1943 municipal letter, and explicitly says the exact founding year is unknown. This is properly hedged and consistent with the source.",
        "dynastyCheck": "HOLDS as a branch attribution, with one internal conflation to flag. Otynia (Otynia/Aotinia) is genuinely a daughter-branch of Vizhnitz, and the 1943 letter is signed by the gabbai of the \"Vizhnitz-Otynia\" synagogue per Glatter, so the dynasty label is correct and beats the map's \"Slonim.\" HOWEVER the Glatter INDEX lists the rebbe for this Rashi entry as \"Rabbi Eliezer Hager\" - that is a conflation: the actual Otynia rebbe was Israel Shalom Yosef Hager (Chaim's son, murdered in the Holocaust), while Eliezer Hager (Damesek Eliezer) was the main Vizhnitz rebbe at Pierberg 35. The research JSON correctly identifies this in its gaps section as \"probably a generic Vizhnitz attribution, not the local shtibel rabbi\" and does NOT propagate the Eliezer Hager error into its founder/rebbe fields. Good adversarial discipline by the original researcher.",
        "imageCheck": "No image was included, and that is the correct call. No free-licensed verified portrait of the Otynia rebbe was confirmed, and per the \"when in doubt, no image\" rule the JSON omitted it. No fabricated image URL present. Nothing to flag.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "Map's house number 'Rashi 1' is UNSUPPORTED - Glatter gives no house number; treat as unconfirmed map artifact.",
          "Map's dynasty label 'Slonim' at Rashi street is WRONG - Slonim rebbe Weinberg lived/ran his beit midrash on Tiomkin street, never Rashi. Correct dynasty is Vizhnitz-Otynia.",
          "Glatter INDEX's 'rebbe: Eliezer Hager' for the Rashi/Otynia entry is a likely conflation (Eliezer Hager = main Vizhnitz, Pierberg 35; actual Otynia rebbe was Israel Shalom Yosef Hager). The research JSON correctly does NOT adopt this error.",
          "currentStatus 'unknown' is honest - no independent online record of the shtibel's present existence or closure was found; cannot be resolved.",
          "Warning correctly noted in JSON: do not confuse with the separate Vizhnitz synagogue on Rashi street in BNEI BRAK (different city, 1980s-2000s)."
        ],
        "corrections": "1) Drop or explicitly mark the house number: Glatter documents only \"Rashi street,\" no number, so \"Rashi 1\" cannot be asserted - the JSON already hedges this; keep it hedged. 2) The map's \"Slonim\" attribution at this address is the actual error and should be corrected to Vizhnitz-Otynia (Slonim's Weinberg was on Tiomkin street, confirmed via He-Wikipedia). 3) Note the Glatter index's internal inconsistency: it tags the Rashi entry rebbe as \"Eliezer Hager,\" which conflates the Otynia shtibel with the main Vizhnitz court; the true Otynia rebbe line ran through Israel Shalom Yosef Hager. The research JSON handled this correctly by refusing to name a local rebbe. 4) Where Glatter and open-web reasoning meet, they AGREE here: both independently support a Vizhnitz-Otynia presence on Rashi street and a Slonim presence on Tiomkin, so no override conflict. 5) Overall the research JSON is well-disciplined: properly hedged on the number, the founding year, the local rebbe name, and the image; its only residual risk is the unconfirmable \"Rashi 1\" inherited from the map."
