        "addressCheck": "No support for Hakongres 25. Glatter's Gur entry (type beit-midrash) has NO street and NO house number - only the general archival ref (אעת\"א, חטיבה 8, מיכל 2331, תיק 30-1960-2) for \"16 בתי תפילה בראשית תש\"ך (1960)\". So Glatter does NOT override geography here - it never places Gur at any address. Open web independently confirms the real Gur addresses are פיירברג 17 (Tel Aviv Religious Council / rabanut.co.il) and הדף היומי in Neve Sharett (Kipa), plus historically בר אילן/פיירברג/יבנה (Time Out). project-tlv's Hakongres page lists only ONE synagogue on the street - פועלי צדק at הקונגרס 21 / צ'לנוב 31 (a non-Hasidic workers' synagogue) - and nothing at #25. The claim's own conclusion (no Gur institution at this address; likely map/coordinate confusion) is CORRECT.",
        "sourceQuality": "Good and honest. All 5 cited sources resolve and support the negative conclusion: rabanut.co.il gives פיירברג 17 for Gur; Kipa gives the Neve-Sharett/Hadaf HaYomi Gur shtiblach; project-tlv confirms only פועלי צדק (#21) on Hakongres and nothing at #25; Time Out lists Gur on בר אילן/פיירברג/יבנה. No fabricated or dead links found. The Glatter archival ref is reproduced accurately and honestly flagged as address-less (no invented file number for #25). This is a responsibly-built \"non-verified\" entry rather than a fabrication.",
        "dynastyCheck": "Dynasty attribution to Gur (Ger) is accurate as historical background (confirmed via Wikipedia/YIVO), but there is NO institution to attribute it to at this address - it is dynasty-elsewhere, not site-specific. The claim correctly does not assert a real Gur site at #25.",
        "founderCheck": "Dynasty founder correctly named: רבי יצחק מאיר אלתר (חידושי הרי\"ם), who established the Ger court in Góra Kalwaria after the Kotzker Rebbe's death (1859); successors שפת אמת (יהודה אריה לייב אלתר) and אמרי אמת (אברהם מרדכי אלתר) - all confirmed. BUT no founder is or can be tied to THIS address, and the claim honestly states founder = unknown for the site.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "Year is \"unknown\" - defensible, since no institution exists at this address. No anachronism introduced. The dynasty founding context (1859, Poland) is correctly kept separate from the Tel Aviv site.",
