        "sourceQuality": "Mixed. Strong: Calcalist investigative feature and the JGive nonprofit registry both directly document \"בית החסידים דגור נחמני 58\" — these are the load-bearing sources and they resolve and support the corrected address. Hebrew Wikipedia (חסידות גור / האדמו\"ר מגור / ישראל אלתר) reliably supports the dynasty background, the founding year 1859, the founder (Chidushei HaRim), and the succession. The image source (Wikimedia Commons File:Imrei_Emes.jpg) is genuine, a real pre-1948 portrait photograph, public domain (copyright expired). WEAK/MISLEADING: the cited rabanut.co.il (Tel Aviv Religious Council) \"חסידי גור\" page does NOT list Nachmani at all — it gives the address as פיירברג 17 (Fierberg 17). So that source is cited as support for a Nachmani Gur institution but actually documents a DIFFERENT Gur location. The Ynet \"שינקין\" source is general color, not address-specific.",
