        "dynastyCheck": "Correct. Gur (גור / Ger), originating in Góra Kalwaria, Poland; founded by R. Yitzchak Meir Alter (Chidushei HaRim); continued by Sfat Emet and Imrei Emet; in the relevant period led by R. Yisrael Alter (\"Beis Yisrael\"). All verified against both Wikipedia articles and the Glatter index, which independently lists Gur as the largest Hasidic core in Tel Aviv. No conflation with another dynasty.",
        "founderCheck": "Honest and defensible. The research does NOT invent a named human founder for this specific shtibel — it attributes it to \"the local Gur Hasidim (Beit HaChasidim DeGur)\" and notes the sitting rebbe was R. Yisrael Alter (Beis Yisrael), correctly placing him in Jerusalem, outside Tel Aviv. This avoids the common fabrication trap. Yisrael Alter is a real, verified figure (5th Gur rebbe, 1948–1977, immigrated 1940, d. 20 Feb 1977). No fabricated founder.",
