        "dynastyCheck": "SOLID. Vaslui (ווסלוי/וסלוי) is a real Ruzhin-house dynasty founded in Vaslui, Romania by R. Shalom Halperin, grandson of R. Yisrael Friedman of Ruzhin (mother Leah, daughter of the Ruzhiner) and son-in-law of R. Yitzchak Friedman of Bohush. Confirmed by he.wikipedia, en.wikipedia, hamichlol, jewiki. The claim correctly attaches the Bohush son-in-law relationship to the FOUNDER Shalom Halperin (not a conflation). Yaakov Yosef Shlomo himself married Sarah Devorah bat R. Yaakov Shimshon Kaner per hamichlol; the claim does not misassign this. Glatter independently lists dynasty \"ווסלוי (Vaslui)\" with rebbe Halperin — attribution holds in both web and Glatter.",
        "founderCheck": "SOLID for the institution. Founder of the Tel Aviv beit midrash is correctly R. Yaakov Yosef Shlomo Halperin, the Vaslui rebbe (b. 5 Elul 5662/1902, d. 11 Tevet 5685/Jan 1985, buried Nachalat Yitzhak, Tel Aviv) — a real person specifically tied to THIS address (he opened the Ben-Gurion synagogue and made it the Israeli Vaslui center; son/successor Avraham Shimshon Shalom Halperin, b.1943, still runs daily prayers/lessons in the father's house there). Glatter independently names the same rebbe. Genealogy Shalom → Chaim Dov → Yaakov Yosef Shlomo → Avraham Shimshon Shalom confirmed; claim's \"grandson of Shalom Halperin\" is correct.",
