        "corrections": "1) Address: The map's 'פרץ אוניקובסקי 13' is wrong in BOTH street and number. The historic location was a rented 3-room building at רחוב פרץ 12 (number 12, not 13), in south Tel Aviv near the old central bus station, occupied from תרצ\\\"ט/1939. There is no street named 'פרץ אוניקובסקי'; the refinement to 'י.ל. פרץ 12' is a plausible inference but sources state only 'פרץ'. 2) Earliest home: before Peretz 12, the yeshiva started (1936) in the Gur shtibel on רחוב התבור (Tabor St) — add this; the research skips it. 3) Founding year: keep תרצ\\\"ו/1936 for the founding, but do NOT conflate it with the 1939 Peretz-12 move; permanent building inaugurated 1953. 4) Founder: soften to 'established by R. Simcha Bunim Alter (Lev Simcha) under the direction of his father the Imrei Emes per the yeshiva\\\\'s account; first rosh yeshiva was R. Gedalia Hertz; R. Simcha Bunim later served as president.' 5) Coordinates: the map coordinates are wrong (point to Ramat Aviv); neither historic (south TA) nor current (Ramat HaChayil) site is at those coords. 6) Current address נמירוב/נמירובר 24, רמת החייל is correct. 7) Note that Glatter does NOT supply an address for this yeshiva, so it cannot 'override' anything geographic here — the dynasty/name match is all Glatter confirms. Image and dynasty attribution are correct as-is."
