        "overallVerdict": "mostly-solid",
        "founderCheck": "REAL and specifically tied to Jaffa. Rabbi Chaim Mordechai Rosenbaum (\"הדבר חיים\") is a real Nadvorna rebbe who, per Hebrew Wikipedia, HaMichlol, and the Nadvorna-dynasty Wikipedia article, moved to Jaffa during the War of Independence and there founded the yeshiva \"מאמר מרדכי - נדבורנה\" (~1949). Hebrew Wikipedia (dynasty): \"הוקמה ביפו על ידי רבי חיים מרדכי רוזנבוים.\" So the founder IS tied to this institution and to Jaffa specifically, not merely the dynasty elsewhere. BUT the research's identity metadata is wrong in two ways: (a) it gives his dates as 1883–1977 — actual dates are 1903–1978 (born Czernowitz, died Bnei Brak 15 Tevet 5738); (b) it calls Itamar Rosenbaum his \"brother/family member (אחיו/בן המשפחה)\" — Itamar (1886–1973) was his FATHER. Note Glatter itself gets this right: \"רבי איתמר רוזנבוים ובנו חיים מרדכי\" (Itamar AND HIS SON Chaim Mordechai), contradicting the research's \"brother\" framing.",
        "foundingYearCheck": "~1949 is DEFENSIBLE. Hebrew Wikipedia and HaMichlol state the move to Jaffa happened during the War of Independence (1948–49) and the yeshiva was founded after statehood; secondary sources give 1949 for the \"Maamar Mordechai\" yeshiva, with the move to Jerusalem in 1950 (תש\"י). The sequence Jaffa ~1949 -> Jerusalem 1950 -> Bnei Brak 1960 is consistent across Wikipedia, HaMichlol, and Glatter (Glatter's \"1950 Jerusalem\" matches the Jerusalem phase). No anachronism in the year.",
        "dynastyCheck": "Dynasty attribution HOLDS: Nadvorna (נדבורנה), origin in Nadvirna, East Galicia. Confirmed by all sources and by Glatter (entry \"נדבורנה ... רבי איתמר רוזנבוים ובנו חיים מרדכי\"). One caveat: the research names the dynasty's founder as \"רבי מרדכי לייפר מנדבורנה.\" Mordechai Leifer (1824–1894) is the eponymous/most famous founder and author of \"מאמר מרדכי\" (after which the yeshiva is named, and he is Chaim Mordechai's grandfather — both confirmed). However Hebrew Wikipedia traces the dynasty's start to an earlier ancestor (Yissachar Ber Leifer). Calling Mordechai Leifer \"the founder\" is the common popular attribution and defensible, but technically he is the dynasty's defining figure rather than its first rebbe. Grandfather claim (Mordechai of Nadvorna) and the yeshiva being named for his book \"מאמר מרדכי\" are both CONFIRMED.",
        "addressCheck": "Glatter does NOT support a Jaffa street/house number. The Glatter Nadvorna entry is type \"rebbe-home\" with origin \"ירושלים (Jerusalem)\", year 1950, and NO street, NO number, NO archival file reference — it documents the Jerusalem phase, not Jaffa, and never mentions Hassan Bek/Manshiyya. The research's claimed pin location \"חסאן בק / מנשייה ביפו\" is supported by NO source (web or Glatter). The Jaffa CITY-level location is well-documented; the specific Hassan Bek/Manshiyya ADDRESS is not. Research correctly self-flags this as \"unverifiable\" and correctly notes Glatter places Nadvorna in Jerusalem (1950), not Jaffa. Where Glatter and the open-web differ: web sources support Jaffa as the first stop, Glatter only records the later Jerusalem home — these are complementary, not contradictory, since Glatter simply doesn't catalog the brief Jaffa phase. Neither supports Hassan Bek.",
        "imageCheck": "Correctly handled — NO image attached, and that is the right call. Web search surfaced only a tombstone/gravesite file (File:ציוני האדמורים מנדבורנה.JPG) and no verified free-licensed PORTRAIT photograph. Per the \"if unsure, no image\" rule, omitting the image is correct. No fabricated image URL present (images array is empty). Good.",
        "sourceQuality": "Cited URLs resolve and genuinely support the core claims. Hebrew Wikipedia \"חיים מרדכי רוזנבוים\", \"חסידות נדבורנה\", \"איתמר רוזנבוים\", and HaMichlol all loaded and confirm: Nadvorna dynasty, Jaffa founding of \"מאמר מרדכי\" yeshiva ~1949, Jerusalem 1950, Bnei Brak 1960. Sources are tertiary (Wikipedia/HaMichlol/Michlol) rather than academic, but adequate and mutually corroborating. Glatter is the only source with archival file numbers, but it has none for Nadvorna. The cited pnimi.org.il dynasty link in the broader web (story page) returned 404 but was not in the JSON's source list, so no broken cited link.",
        "flaggedClaims": [
          "FABRICATED ADDRESS: 'חסאן בק / מנשייה ביפו' as the pin location — supported by NO source; research itself admits this is undocumented (correctly flagged unverifiable).",
          "WRONG DATES: Chaim Mordechai given as 1883–1977; actual 1903–1978 (Hebrew Wikipedia & HaMichlol: born תרס\"ג/1903 Czernowitz, died ט\"ו טבת תשל\"ח/1978 Bnei Brak).",
          "WRONG RELATIONSHIP / CONFLATION: research calls Itamar Rosenbaum the 'brother/family member (אחיו)' of Chaim Mordechai. Itamar (1886–1973) was his FATHER. Glatter itself states 'איתמר רוזנבוים ובנו חיים מרדכי' (father and son), contradicting the research.",
          "WRONG IMMIGRATION YEAR for Itamar: research says he made aliyah '1967/תשכ\"ט'. 1967 = תשכ\"ז, not תשכ\"ט; Hebrew Wikipedia gives תשכ\"ט = 1969. Year/Hebrew-year mismatch.",
          "OVERSTATED FOUNDER claim: 'רבי מרדכי לייפר' as dynasty founder — he is the eponymous/defining rebbe (1824–1894), but Hebrew Wikipedia traces the line to an earlier ancestor; defensible but imprecise.",
          "Glatter origin 'Jerusalem 1950' reflects the Jerusalem phase and does NOT corroborate the Jaffa pin, contrary to any reading that Glatter 'confirms' the Jaffa institution's location."
        ],
        "corrections": "1) Fix dates: Rabbi Chaim Mordechai Rosenbaum = 1903–1978 (NOT 1883–1977). 2) Fix relationship: Itamar Rosenbaum (1886–1973) was his FATHER, not brother; both Glatter and Hebrew Wikipedia confirm father-son. 3) Fix Itamar's aliyah: תשכ\"ט = 1969 (not 1967); he settled in Yad Eliyahu, Tel Aviv (this part is correct). 4) Address: do NOT assert Hassan Bek/Manshiyya — keep as 'Jaffa, exact location undocumented'; the city is supported, the street is not, and Glatter has no street/number for Nadvorna. 5) Keep mapErrorFlag 'unverifiable' (correct). 6) Founding year ~1949 is fine. 7) Dynasty = Nadvorna is correct; grandfather Mordechai of Nadvorna and yeshiva named after his book 'מאמר מרדכי' are correct. 8) Consider noting Mordechai Leifer is the dynasty's defining figure rather than strictly its first rebbe. 9) Image correctly omitted — leave empty. Net: the institution, founder, dynasty, and ~1949 Jaffa founding are SOLID; the person's birth/death dates and the Itamar relationship are FABRICATED/CONFLATED and must be corrected; the Hassan Bek address remains unsupported."
